{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion","id":117347,"title":"Idigam Chronicles General Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-21T20:10:41-07:00","id":117347,"title":"Idigam Chronicles General Discussion","content":"In an attempt to keep things relevant to the actual themed threads, I figured this one would do for musings and general chat about the upcoming release. This thread would also be a better fit for discussion about general themes such as perceived power compared to other archetypes despite it technically being related to topics such as forms, gifts, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 04-21-2014, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T22:40:44-07:00","id":117424,"title":"","content":"Here's a general theme: I strongly disapprove of the constant use of First Tongue terminology, especially when compared to the old game, which used it only lightly. While I love the First Tongue - it adds a great feel of timelessness and ancient beauty to the setting - I think it's been used too often to the point that accessibility of the game suffers, especially for people who might be new to the game.<br /> <br /> I prefer &quot;Death Rage&quot; over &quot;Kuruth&quot;, &quot;Sacred Hunt&quot; over &quot;Siskur-Dah&quot; and &quot;werewolf&quot; over &quot;Uratha&quot;, really. Especially werewolf. As Ethan Skemp said in his writers bible a long time ago, do use the word &quot;werewolf&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T23:27:50-07:00","id":117445,"title":"","content":"One of the strengths of the WoD series, in my personal experience, is that they try to keep you immersed even when you're reading them from a technical standpoint. So I run the opposite direction when it comes to the constant use of First Tongue. I find it immensely rewarding to commit key terms and important phrases to memory, it's immersing to me. Being able to fluidly slip in some First Tongue into dialogue is an incredibly gratifying roleplaying experience.<br /> <br /> Also not to insult some of the people I've played with before, but generally the people who get confused by the First Tongue terminology sprinkled around are the same people who need help filling out their character sheet. Players that have spent the time reading, again in my personal experience, don't have an issue with the constant use of First Tongue.<br /> <br /> As long as they provide the translation in the sections of the book that matter to character creation and don't start forming whole sentences in First Tongue by stringing words together, I have zero issue with the direction things are going in this respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T00:59:30-07:00","id":117467,"title":"","content":"I don't see a problem with the book using First Tongue on a regular basis. Simply on the grounds of basic writing style, variation is nice. Using werewolf every time or Death Rage every time is fairly clunky. Having a variety of terms helps break that up. Having part of that variety being the First Tongue words helps keep the intent clear.<br /> <br /> I think this also touches on something that's been a constant thing with the spoilers: we're getting snippets without the total context of the book. We don't know how First Tongue heavy the Idigam Chronicle will be compared to the original Forsaken core by just a few test-document level drafts. Maybe once the full book is together and can be edited as one that will get toned back because it comes off too heavily First Tongue happy. Maybe that isn't really going to be a problem. But it's a bit premature to take issue with something when we don't have the total context.<br /> <br /> On of the reasons I haven't bothered saying anything on the Gifts thread is because there really isn't enough context to hang much on. Besides the new Gift structuring, things like Renown and &quot;overall power level&quot; are still up in the air until we see things like Form, Rituals, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T09:10:33-07:00","id":117485,"title":"","content":"A question for the developer and writers: In Blood and moke there were a lot of vampiric domains. In Idigam Chronicles we know there will be the Tokyo Hunting Ground, but which other hunting grounds we'll see? Will you pot some entry on the blog about some of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T11:07:18-07:00","id":117544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117424#post117424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer &quot;Death Rage&quot; over &quot;Kuruth&quot;, &quot;Sacred Hunt&quot; over &quot;Siskur-Dah&quot; and &quot;werewolf&quot; over &quot;Uratha&quot;, really. Especially werewolf. As Ethan Skemp said in his writers bible a long time ago, do use the word &quot;werewolf&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it, Werewolf is a descriptor, it is what the humans call them. Uratha is the people and what they refer to themselves as. Why? First of all, it is older and they don't see themselves are cursed which Werewolf carries the connotation of. Second, it is exactly the same as how Vampires call themselves Kindred rather than Vampires...unless the situation seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> Kuruth and Siskur-Dah hold similar connotations. Death rage is merely a lousy interpretation of Kuruth as you can have Kuruth without being near death. Siskur-Dah is the act of the pack or individual hunting his prey, while Sacred Hunt sounds more like a holy procedure.<br /> <br /> I hearken the First-Tongue versions to the actual meaning where translation is impossible although similar<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:51:09-07:00","id":117702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117485#post117485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question for the developer and writers: In Blood and moke there were a lot of vampiric domains. In Idigam Chronicles we know there will be the Tokyo Hunting Ground, but which other hunting grounds we'll see? Will you pot some entry on the blog about some of them?</div> </div> </div> </div> Stew has already said there will be several Hunting Grounds in the book. I can't say where at this stage, but is imagine they will come up in the development blog at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:55:35-07:00","id":117704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117702#post117702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Stew has already said there will be several Hunting Grounds in the book. I can't say where at this stage, but is imagine they will come up in the development blog at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really, really, REALLY hope The Rockies gets revisited. I loved it the first time around, and while I'd understand if the idea is to focus on new places this time around rather than revisiting old ones, the Rockies was just such an iconic setting for Forsaken to me, it would be a shame not to see it return in the new core. Then again, I'm from Denver, so I'm biased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T17:41:48-07:00","id":117752,"title":"","content":"I hope Miami gets one. I really enjoy it for my own games, it's a bit different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T18:41:03-07:00","id":117770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117752#post117752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope Miami gets one. I really enjoy it for my own games, it's a bit different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Florida is probably a bit too messed up spiritually for any Uratha to live there. The spirit of people doing crazy things in Florida is probably rank 10 by now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T20:57:58-07:00","id":117825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117770#post117770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Florida is probably a bit too messed up spiritually for any Uratha to live there. The spirit of people doing crazy things in Florida is probably rank 10 by now</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, it's not THAT bad here.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T22:48:51-07:00","id":117862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117825#post117825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, it's not THAT bad here.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How bad is it then?<br /> P.S. You knew that was coming <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, does anyone else besides me find the statement by Acrozatarim stating that a tank would be insufficient to stop a rampaging Rahu pretty sweet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T23:03:28-07:00","id":117866,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how my prospective players would be able to handle it, but I actually really dig the proliferation of First Tongue stuff because something about the structure of the language makes it easy to say and easy to remember. I'd probably have a printout sheet with a lexicon if I could find it, but I have a much, much better handle on First Tongue than I have with, say, the Ancient Egyptian in MtC.<br /> <br /> And yeah, with all the focus on the hunt I'm actually pretty excited to see the Hunting Grounds in Idigam Chronicles so I can see just how you can stretch that meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T23:27:18-07:00","id":117871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117770#post117770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Florida is probably a bit too messed up spiritually for any Uratha to live there. The spirit of people doing crazy things in Florida is probably rank 10 by now</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imagine Detroit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T03:47:47-07:00","id":117926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117424#post117424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a general theme: I strongly disapprove of the constant use of First Tongue terminology, especially when compared to the old game, which used it only lightly. While I love the First Tongue - it adds a great feel of timelessness and ancient beauty to the setting - I think it's been used too often to the point that accessibility of the game suffers, especially for people who might be new to the game.<br /> <br /> I prefer &quot;Death Rage&quot; over &quot;Kuruth&quot;, &quot;Sacred Hunt&quot; over &quot;Siskur-Dah&quot; and &quot;werewolf&quot; over &quot;Uratha&quot;, really. Especially werewolf. As Ethan Skemp said in his writers bible a long time ago, do use the word &quot;werewolf&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that - this was one of little things that put me ( and some other people ) off the <b>Forsaken</b>. Whole idea of changing Mother Luna and Father Wolf in <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> spoilers, or chaning he/ she in text for <b>Blood and Smoke</b> were good things.<br /> <br /> I would much prefer interchanging whole First Toung conotatin with the same amount of &quot;normal&quot; talk. So in one sentance &quot;Uratha&quot;, in second &quot;werewolves&quot;. In one Siskur-Dah, in second &quot;Sacred Hunt&quot;.<br /> <br /> And titles of subchapters written like this:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Kuruth, the Death Rage</b></i><br /> <br /> In this way it's both informative ( it has English, expilict meaning in text ) and immersive. Overdoing of Frist Tounge terms what was in previous book looked like <b>Mysterium</b>'s lexicon - beautiful, but usable only for specific type of players. And even my years old <b>Mage</b> players don't use all more causal terminology on play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-24-2014, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T09:09:03-07:00","id":117939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117871#post117871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Imagine Detroit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not THAT bad!<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe it is...I feel like we've got all the crazies down here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T09:11:05-07:00","id":117940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117866#post117866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how my prospective players would be able to handle it, but I actually really dig the proliferation of First Tongue stuff because something about the structure of the language makes it easy to say and easy to remember. I'd probably have a printout sheet with a lexicon if I could find it, but I have a much, much better handle on First Tongue than I have with, say, the Ancient Egyptian in MtC.<br /> <br /> And yeah, with all the focus on the hunt I'm actually pretty excited to see the Hunting Grounds in Idigam Chronicles so I can see just how you can stretch that meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I also had more problems with MtC's terminology than Forsaken's First Tongue, where the words seemed to slip off more easily and were quite easy to remember","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T10:19:20-07:00","id":117979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=117939#post117939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not THAT bad! Okay, maybe it is...I feel like we've got all the crazies down here</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know, I think it would be an Iron Master's paradise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:26:01-07:00","id":118050,"title":"","content":"Miami's a big place, but fairly new. It's...different from Detroit. The government filed bankruptcy back around 2000, but in less than ten years were one of the richest cities in the world (with a caveat).<br /> One of the other big things is we get a lot of people from a lot of different places, but unlike most of them, we don't really become a melting pot, people just keep their own cultural heritage, usually without altering it or meshing with others (this can cause a lot of problems, back in the 80s we had a lot of riots).<br /> We got the beach, a big shipping industry, no basements (the land is very low, and in many places digging that far would just lead to flooding, the sewers are more cramped, as well). Since the real estate thing we've had a lot of neighborhoods full of unfinished or empty houses. Major international hub for trade, lots of ships going out, there's the Free Trade Zone, the Everglades (which are huge), colleges, lots of people for Spring Break, hurricanes (nice st event there), islands within a days travel. I'd think there's a surprising amount of nature spirits for a city, and a nice mix of helions (sunshine state) and lunes<br /> <br /> From a storytelling standpoint, the only problems are the multilingualism (so you're better off letting players know they might need other languages), the lack of history (city's not much more than a hundred years old, and much was uninhabitable swampland before then), and you can't have underground sewer crawls and stereotypical underground lairs without a lot of handwaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-23-2014, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[