,"content":"What cities are you guys hoping for? That was honestly the best bit of B&amp;S for me and I'm excited to see what gets picked for Werewolf and Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:32:04-07:00","id":120143,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see something for Cairo, actually. No real reason, I just think it'd be a very different Werewolf setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:52:07-07:00","id":120156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=120143#post120143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see something for Cairo, actually. No real reason, I just think it'd be a very different Werewolf setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rage Across The World made Werewolf in Cairo sound like a blast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:07:53-07:00","id":120165,"title":"","content":"I have my person vote in for Werewolves in the far north somewhere inside the arctic circle. Think of all of the freedom a pack could have in the less dense population areas where the hunt is a true hunt across the icy wastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:59:29-07:00","id":120191,"title":"","content":"Lets see.<br /> Miami, Florida. Juarez, Mexico. Phnom Penh, Cambodia. I'd like to see some more about the Lodge of Wires, so the San Francisco Bay Area, Silicon Valley or Edinburgh would fit. Calcutta, India.<br /> <br /> I guess there's a few things I like to explore, though they didn't inform everything on the list. A history that would leave the Shadow of the area drastically different from other places, though more through culture clashes. A place where a wolf doesn't really fit, avoiding an interchangeable city surrounded by grasslands and temperate deciduous forest, and I like the tropics, a place in the Caribbean would be cool. Deserts have an appeal, though wolves would fit more. Some place routinely hit by hurricanes, earthquakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-27-2014, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T23:14:02-07:00","id":120200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=119924#post119924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dudes of Legend must have been <i>terrible</i> for you, Hamster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never read it. But as &quot;joke fun splat&quot; I could laugh loud on it. Problem is when laughable elements go to corebook... ( If jokes and fun thing go to supplements it's okay - just jokes in horror game shouldn't, like to say, <i>start</i> a percept for players )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T00:11:48-07:00","id":120223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=119240#post119240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AJNn1y4adkk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AJNn1y4adkk</a><br /> <br /> Because everyone needs more GARO in their life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, I think I may have run across this before and then completely and utterly forgotten about it.<br /> <br /> Actually for the anime experienced, I have had a couple of people recommend Wolfs Rain as a good media example for Forsaken (I do believe it was actually recommended in the book itself). I've never got around to watching it though. Found out the English voice cast and recording are the same guys that did Cowboy Bebop though, which is selling me on giving it a shot. Any additional points you guys can raise about it as a selling point?<br /> <br /> As for locations, I'd like Cape Town, Cairo, Sydney, Mexico City and Athens. I know that all sounds pretty random, but I found the more &quot;neglected&quot; areas (in Requiems publishing history) to be the most interesting in Blood and Smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T00:30:12-07:00","id":120226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=120223#post120223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually for the anime experienced, I have had a couple of people recommend Wolfs Rain as a good media example for Forsaken (I do believe it was actually recommended in the book itself). I've never got around to watching it though. Found out the English voice cast and recording are the same guys that did Cowboy Bebop though, which is selling me on giving it a shot. Any additional points you guys can raise about it as a selling point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wached whole Wolf's Rain when I had Werewolf hype, few years ago. It's good series, only that it's have like 6 real episodes - rest of series is rerospective on previous things from other point of view. But good watch, none the less. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And opening song is one of my favorite's of all time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/xoQuu7GPxAI\" data-code=\"xoQuu7GPxAI\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xoQuu7GPxAI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T10:27:43-07:00","id":120402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=119161#post119161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'm having the <i>hilarious</i> image of Sailor Moon... if you replaced the Sailor Senshi with Uratha.<br /> <br /> Kind of gives new meaning to &quot;In the name of the Moon, I will punish you&quot;, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I and my group have been using that as a joke since we first bought Forsaken, which was about the same time as.. eh.. Armory came out. We still think it's hilarious.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow, I'd really like to see some city in Scandinavia. Not only because I'm from here (although I admit it IS a huge bonus for me) but because there is quite a bit of the Norse about the Uratha. Fenris being one of the First-Born, and Garm being, just like in the myths, one of his sons. There is also the lodge of the Maelstrom, and the Valkyrja Mot. Nordic kinda fits. The Werewolf packs are also reminiscent of the old clans here. Your family is the family that chooses you. Often it's something you are born into, but if you are ever adopted into a family, that IS your family. And I keep getting the same vibes from Werewolf packs. Not to mention berserker soldiers, which also fits.<br /> <br /> Thus, I'd like to see Stockholm or Oslo. Perhaps Helsinki, it isn't Viking, but it's still pretty close. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":585,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","user":"Seidmadr","date":".  Decided to fill out a post, instead of double-posting 04-27-2014, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:31:02-07:00","id":120422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=120402#post120402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyhow, I'd really like to see some city in Scandinavia. Not only because I'm from here (although I admit it IS a huge bonus for me) but because there is quite a bit of the Norse about the Uratha. Fenris being one of the First-Born, and Garm being, just like in the myths, one of his sons. There is also the lodge of the Maelstrom, and the Valkyrja Mot. Nordic kinda fits. The Werewolf packs are also reminiscent of the old clans here. Your family is the family that chooses you. Often it's something you are born into, but if you are ever adopted into a family, that IS your family. And I keep getting the same vibes from Werewolf packs. Not to mention berserker soldiers, which also fits.<br /> <br /> Thus, I'd like to see Stockholm or Oslo. Perhaps Helsinki, it isn't Viking, but it's still pretty close. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Stealling those ideas for my prepered <b>Werewolf</b> game tom ake it non-US and cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-27-2014, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:51:54-07:00","id":120471,"title":"","content":"Still working on my Kosovo setting. Places where atrocities have happened <i>very</i> recently work unsurprisingly well for Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T17:46:28-07:00","id":120634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=120402#post120402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus, I'd like to see Stockholm or Oslo. Perhaps Helsinki, it isn't Viking, but it's still pretty close. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Me too! Mainly because of 1) the great ideas here and in the Uratha Culture thread, 2) I'm such a Scandinavia-buff, and 3) <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gXN9acC9edU\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> can be the theme song <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T21:21:27-07:00","id":120724,"title":"","content":"I don't know if comes from having grown up in a country with a phonetic language (Wales) taught alongside English but I never had any issue with First Tongue. I treat it as an entirely phonetic language like Welsh and have never had any issue with it. <br /> <br /> I find the Egyptian terms in Mummy much, much more problematic. The way I pronounced Shaunkshen for a while was brutal until I heard and interview where the developer pronounced it. I don't think Mummy even provided a phonetic break down of its words. Werewolf meanwhile always has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T12:59:19-07:00","id":121922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=120724#post120724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if comes from having grown up in a country with a phonetic language (Wales) taught alongside English but I never had any issue with First Tongue. I treat it as an entirely phonetic language like Welsh and have never had any issue with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finnish here, and neither have I ever had problems with first tongue. I think only the more unknown sounds (Z's, X's) are harder, but for example Imnir and Meninna, idigam and so are easy as pie.<br /> <br /> Now for my own takes;<br /> <br /> * Refocus on the wolf: Oh man is it here, I'm loving how much more the focus is on the fact that the characters are hunters, not warriors. And that humanity vs feral creature is now more the focus.<br /> <br /> *New Harmony is not based on the Oath: This was one of my biggest gripes about Forsaken. Any ambiguity of their wars and issues is taken away by looking at the Harmony chart essentially following the oath. So the Pure are of course wrong. Another reason why it stunk was that it made the intrepentation of these laws essentially pointless from tribe to tribe. Now, it is more about actual balance, and punishes going too far on either side.<br /> <br /> *Wolf-Blooded are not kinfolk: Another correction I just love. As a mainly online gamer, I have seen wolf-blooded become essentially kinfolk 2.0 in games. As much as I like kinfolk in certain situations, I much rather not have them in Forsaken. Now, Wolf-Blooded are truly -wolf- blooded, with their changes being random, their nature is no longer so clear. The fact that they can shapeshift, they can be a walking locus,etc. make being one much more a curse/blessing thing. And as noted in other threads, now players who want traditional werewolves..get traditional werewolves.<br /> <br /> *Tribes focus on prey: My most common voiced complaint about Forsaken is how new uratha join tribes, if the game is bottom up. And why? In a simple move, it is explained, tribes have favoured prey and so an uratha joins tribe to focus on that. That takes away so much of the confusion why, because in a society of hunters,specialization is extremely good. Also, Iron Masters being human hunters is awesome, giving their city-ness a new sinister feel.<br /> <br /> *Packs can be whatever the Uratha wish it to be: Bottom up society, right? Well, often in the later books (plus in play) I felt the Uratha society was still there. Now that packs seem to be more what each pack wants it to be, say some members are animals, some WBs, some humans, a pack is less an uratha only club and more a gaggle of friends. NWoD shines in its freedom to have whatever it wishes, without pre-established canon to weight crossover interactions down, this also means crossover just got a lot more fun ^^<br /> <br /> Edit: Wolf-born=Wolf-blooded XP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 04-29-2014, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T22:25:44-07:00","id":122200,"title":"","content":"Disliking much of what I've seen so far about the Idigam Chronicle, especially Harmony, the Cahalith auspice and gifts. Too early to judge, but it looks to me as if I'll keep on using the Werewolf: the Forsaken setting, and I already have my own system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:34:37-07:00","id":122349,"title":"","content":"See Christian it boggles me that you'd take this stance on it, it so far sounds incredibly brilliant and already set my brain meats into overdrive thinking of awesome scenarios.<br /> <br /> Pack of Predator Kings murders the players human and wolf blooded pack while they're out on a proper hunt...<br /> <br /> Hell seeing as how my two main players are usually an elodoth and irraka (respectively a storm lord and an Iron master) I would think a serial killer being urged / ridden by a murder spirit would make for an amazing storyline. Murder mystery all criminal minds style followed by a right proper hunt from the main characters tracking down what could essentially be jack the ripper or the zodiac killer. <br /> <br /> If anything its added quite a bit to a dramatic perspective and opened the werewolves up for more relate able play, which is all around better. If you can really get into the character then it makes it far funner to play, and I feel this will be the case with Idigam. Hell we might even pick up all the teen fiction reader fans and educate them on proper werewolf fiction while we're at it. And there's nothing wrong with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:39:44-07:00","id":122354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=122349#post122349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See Christian it boggles me that you'd take this stance on it, it so far sounds incredibly brilliant and already set my brain meats into overdrive thinking of awesome scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respect that, and I'm glad that feedback on what's been spoiled so far seems to be positive, mostly. Me, I still have my old Forsaken books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=122349#post122349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pack of Predator Kings murders the players human and wolf blooded pack while they're out on a proper hunt...<br /> <br /> Hell seeing as how my two main players are usually an elodoth and irraka (respectively a storm lord and an Iron master) I would think a serial killer being urged / ridden by a murder spirit would make for an amazing storyline. Murder mystery all criminal minds style followed by a right proper hunt from the main characters tracking down what could essentially be jack the ripper or the zodiac killer.<br /> <br /> If anything its added quite a bit to a dramatic perspective and opened the werewolves up for more relate able play, which is all around better. If you can really get into the character then it makes it far funner to play, and I feel this will be the case with Idigam. Hell we might even pick up all the teen fiction reader fans and educate them on proper werewolf fiction while we're at it. And there's nothing wrong with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't need the Idigam Chronicle book to do any of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:44:50-07:00","id":122359,"title":"","content":"No suppose not, but it did give me further inspiration on what I can do with the characters.<br /> <br /> It looks like most of what the old forsaken books have is still viable according to stew. How much of that will remain true I dunno. We already seem to be missing the Unihar which is a pretty big fundamental change. We'll see what forms do and how that applies, and hopefully the war form is insanely more viable. <br /> <br /> My biggest concerns with Idigam were: making signs of the moon and tribes of the moon completely obsolete. There's so much good material in there it would be a shame to see it negated, and thankfully it does not look to be the case. At least just yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:51:50-07:00","id":122368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=122359#post122359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like most of what the old forsaken books have is still viable according to stew.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but it's not really a defense of the things I don't like about Idigam Chronicle. I don't buy a book about that has things I don't like, when I already have book about werewolves I like a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=122359#post122359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of that will remain true I dunno. We already seem to be missing the Unihar which is a pretty big fundamental change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. Add that to the list of changes I don't like.<br /> <br /> In terms of positivity: I like the new wolf-blooded. I like - after a little consideration - the idea of the Forsaken tribes each having their own particular preferred prey. I've implemented that particular idea in my DRYH Werewolf rules as a &quot;Prey&quot; gift available to all Forsaken.<br /> <br /> That's pretty much it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:57:26-07:00","id":122371,"title":"","content":"Yeah the unihar being removed threw me too. Especially when the breeder seemed like a deliciously evil specimen of Idigam. hopefully the Idigam from lodge of last winter makes it in. I'd love to run a post apocalyptic world where every werewolf is essentially pure tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T09:01:13-07:00","id":122372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=122371#post122371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the unihar being removed threw me too. Especially when the breeder seemed like a deliciously evil specimen of Idigam. hopefully the Idigam from lodge of last winter makes it in. I'd love to run a post apocalyptic world where every werewolf is essentially pure tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I'd rather see them spend precious, precious wordcount on the core setting rather than venture into other genres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T09:10:39-07:00","id":122379,"title":"","content":"Aye, although we already have 15+ books on core setting. I wouldn't mind a little nod of additional info. Especially considering it already got a nod in Tribes and I don't think too many people read about it. <br /> <br /> Things I want to see still in Idigam: Rules. A clear damn explanation of the rules. None of this flip to book a to get the answer for book b nonsense that was big with previous books (they've thankfully changed that)<br /> <br /> A clear presentation on what their werewolves are along with what their auspices mean. Looks like we're already getting that.<br /> <br /> I want to see the Bale Hounds get some much needed love, perhaps their own prey focus amongst other things. Maybe a more cohesive cultural design? I LOVED the 9th tribe concept in blasphemies. <br /> <br /> I want the Pure to receive similar attention as they are not purely antagonists. They are also fully capable of being player characters (as seen in The Pure) and I feel they should at least get a section with some attention to their hunting culture.<br /> <br /> I get that we're trying to get as much crammed into the books as possible, but I think if they were to somehow get funding with the new lines, perhaps they could do something like the &quot;rage across x&quot; series from apocalypse? Hunting grounds, I think, was originally going to be a book line and only got the rockies. Not a bad setting but there are so many more interesting places in the world that they could explore that I feel it would warrant its own book entirely. <br /> <br /> So in thinking in that line, things that Idigam could kick off that I would appreciate: Idigam Chronicle, Hunting Grounds, and a refreshed players guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T09:20:50-07:00","id":122392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=122379#post122379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye, although we already have 15+ books on core setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new people the Idigam Chronicle book is supposed to bring into this hobby don't. The book isn't just for people who already know Werewolf. It's a corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Chris