 rules changes in GMC - but how now spirits are changed? I run both <b>Mage</b> and <b>Werewolf</b> now, so should probably look on new ephemera rules I suppose...</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still fairly similar, but the rules for ghosts and spirits are a bit more uniform now (along with the rules for angels), using a single unified system of Rank, Conditions, Influences, Manifestations, and Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T22:03:58-07:00","id":141249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141240#post141240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably overlooked it, as I only starting to understand all rules changes in GMC - but how now spirits are changed? I run both <b>Mage</b> and <b>Werewolf</b> now, so should probably look on new ephemera rules I suppose...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;As noted earlier, ephemeral beings use the lower of [Power or Finesse] for Defense unless they are Rank 1, in which case they use the higher. <b>They apply Defense against <i>all</i> attacks, even firearms.</b>&quot;<br /> &quot;<b>Physical attacks on a manifest entity that normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane.</b> Despite appearing to the naked eye and being solid, a manifest spirit, ghost, or angel doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T22:36:54-07:00","id":141264,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the bane count as aggravated damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T23:00:05-07:00","id":141272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141264#post141264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't the bane count as aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If the bane has been used as a weapon against the entity, the wounds suffered are aggravated for Manifest entities and lethal for entities still in Twilight.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T00:37:08-07:00","id":141327,"title":"","content":"It's a bit clearer in Idigam Chronicle itself that it's also aggravated when you and the spirit are both in the hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T06:46:05-07:00","id":141513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141215#post141215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain please. Especially considering how GMC fixed the problem of weres needing uzis in shadow to deal with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to tackle this one... Hopefully it makes sense...<br /> <br /> GMC tires very hard to be FATE (At least that is how I see it). That is about as plain as I can say it. And FATE does it better, in my opinion. Tilts, Conditions, etc. are just variations on the FATE Aspect theme. Adding them to the nWOD system just clutters it up in my opinion, because of the Crunch level of nWOD. They are just not needed. Everyone says that the addition of such things made the game more interesting... Combat became more interesting, social situations became more interesting, blah, blah, blah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Problem is, they were never uninteresting in our games to start with. Combat is FAR more epic in base nWOD to me than in GMC. I don't like scrabbling for bonuses just so I can throw 2-3 dice in a combat roll. I don't like that you cannot have an actual graze with a weapon (Case in point - An Axe will always deal a ton of damage, you will never just get a thin red torso cut that you JUST barely managed to connect with for 1 point of lethal in GMC - Hate That, since you can see such things IRL all the time, with both melee and firearms style weapons). It is not Epic to have - Zero Damage, Zero Damage, Zero Damage, 10 Damage and Down. That is just BORING to me.<br /> <br /> On the other Hand, FATE has many of the same things, but their crunch level is so low that they WORK really well. Aspects (Conditions and Tilts in GMC) flow seamlessly and easily throughout the system. Combat is quick, and/or epic when you want it to be. Social Situations can be resolved in exactly the same manner as Combat, just on a social scale, and is quick/epic and/or Slow/subtle when you want it to be, Everything is based upon Intent (which GMC is adding, of course). There is NO grind for abilities or powers like you get in nWOD, since the system is so different (and many things that require powers in nWOD only require you to establish an Aspect in FATE, and it is far easier to get there if you want to do so). In general, if I wanted what GMC is adding in my games, I would just use FATE (Which I am actually doing anyways. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Now, before you think I am bashing GMC, I really am not, I just don't like all the baggage (my opinion) that comes with it. It is convoluted and excessive in my opinion. That being said, the writing has been amazing, and the design team deserves a lot of kudos for that. The fluff is very engaging and entertaining. And I plan on using a lot of it, just not in a GMC style game... I will just back-port it all to base nWOD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> *shrug*<br /> <br /> And for the record - Not once have our werewolves EVER had to resort to firearms to deal with a spirit. NOT ONE TIME (you want to take care of a Rank 4 Spirit and you are a New Pack of Rank 2 Werewolves, YOU DONT FIGHT THE SPIRIT, you go at it from a different angle altogether). So, your issues are obviously not OUR issues when it comes to things like that. Of course, we really don't think things like Gifts, Rites, or even Shapeshifting in Forsaken were broken to start with (though I do like what <i><b>Pendragon </b></i>and others have done with the base alterations/corrections they have added, even if we don't use them - looking at maybe revisiting some of them to fix a few of the niggling disconnects that are there).<br /> <br /> So, I really don't think that GMC actually FIXED anything mechanically, because Mechanically, it was never broken. All GMC did was change how things were mechanically addressed, and to the detriment of the game, in my opinion, since other systems do what they want to do far better than GMC does, and do so in a better narrative space, in my opinion. *shrug* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Does that make any Sense, <i><b>Chattnos</b></i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 05-18-2014, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T07:07:08-07:00","id":141554,"title":"","content":"It is Sunday, even in USA - how long for my spoilers fix? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T07:29:00-07:00","id":141561,"title":"","content":"@ <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein\">Tymeaus Jalynsfein<br /> I get your damage point. I'm just now gearing up for post GMC rules use. I understand the FATE comparisons even if I've never seen that system.<br /> Not sure about tilts myself and need to look at that.<br /> <br /> I don't like weapons adding to your hit. That always irked me. I'll keep your issues in mind. I'm trying to get our old playtest group together to hack quite few things and see how the run. Personally I haven't seen new wolf run but heard those complaints about uzi's in shadow. I'd actually like to see the group try either version of new wolf.<br /> <br /> But I like a lot of the Vamp stuff even if I don't agree with all the fluff. Though going to Mask and Dirge instead Virtue &amp; Vice was strange to me for a game that was trying to get out of Masq's shadow. I hope they don't follow suite with the other splats. What do y'all think of keeping Virtue &amp; Vice in Werewolf?</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T08:37:18-07:00","id":141609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141513#post141513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll try to tackle this one... Hopefully it makes sense...<br /> <br /> GMC tires very hard to be FATE (At least that is how I see it). That is about as plain as I can say it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's wrong, in that GMC has and intends a very different relationship between character and player than FATE goes for.<br /> GMC has taken inspiration from FATE in some specific and small things (arguably, as I can't see into the writers' heads to see where their inspirations come from) but keeps a very different focus through all of it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.penny-arcade.com/discussion/comment/29135084/#Comment_29135084\" target=\"_blank\">This post</a> talking about GMC xp vs FATE points gives a pretty good explanation of the different goals of the systems. At no point does GMC try to go for the more 'third person view' of FATE, it firmly stays with the character.<br /> <br /> Tilts, Aspirations, etc are superficially similar, but are used to evoke a different effect within the system and interact differently with it.<br /> <br /> On a personal note, I tried FATE and intensly disliked it, but really like GMC so far. There is just no point of commonality between the two for me. Nothing in GMC evokes the FATE feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 05-18-2014, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T13:07:28-07:00","id":141762,"title":"","content":"Still no info on this week spoiler? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank"