me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-18-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T14:00:31-07:00","id":141777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141775#post141775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My forum say your post is made at 9:25 PM, and to be true, in Poland now 22:42 ( or just 10:42 PM for you in Americas ). That means that this week Saturday spoiler I will see only on Monday. The spoilers-addiction is very bad for me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> how weird. On my screen it says my post was made at 8:25 PM. I wonder why out times are an hour off. It can't be just the time zone because it's 22:59 where you are and 14:59 where I am...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T14:02:47-07:00","id":141800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141513#post141513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GMC tires very hard to be FATE (At least that is how I see it). That is about as plain as I can say it. And FATE does it better, in my opinion. Tilts, Conditions, etc. are just variations on the FATE Aspect theme. Adding them to the nWOD system just clutters it up in my opinion, because of the Crunch level of nWOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been addressed, I think this is a fairly weak assessment.<br /> <br /> It also disregards that most of these things existing the nWOD previously. The Conditions/Tilts simply gather and codify lots of disparate extant things under a single (or 1.5 anyway) roof, and then tie them into the new XP mechanics. It is really hard to understand it being called &quot;clutter&quot; when it actually organizes and unifies lots of things that already existed.<br /> <br /> As well, the similarities of the Conditions and Aspects systems are very superficial. When you look at how both systems run in detail, and especially how they related to the game point economies, they differentiate heavily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combat is FAR more epic in base nWOD to me than in GMC. I don't like scrabbling for bonuses just so I can throw 2-3 dice in a combat roll. I don't like that you cannot have an actual graze with a weapon (Case in point - An Axe will always deal a ton of damage, you will never just get a thin red torso cut that you JUST barely managed to connect with for 1 point of lethal in GMC - Hate That, since you can see such things IRL all the time, with both melee and firearms style weapons). It is not Epic to have - Zero Damage, Zero Damage, Zero Damage, 10 Damage and Down. That is just BORING to me. </div> </div> </div>I agree that the &quot;no grazing damage without armor or Fighting Merits&quot; thing is one of the weakest aspects of the GMC combat system.<br /> <br /> Otherwise this doesn't make a lot of sense. First off, the nWOD has never been about epic combat. Either version does &quot;epic&quot; well. However... I am having trouble thinking of an &quot;epic&quot; fight involving normal (as in not supernatural) people with heavy weapons that doesn't really come down to lots of rounds of &quot;no meaningful damage done,&quot; until a big hit wins the day.<br /> <br /> An &quot;epic&quot; sniper duel should pretty much end exactly as you describe. The fight ends when one finally gets a hit because they're snipers and when they hit you, you go down.<br /> <br /> An &quot;epic&quot; rapier duel with expert fighters (aka possessing Fight Merits) will likely end up similar to the miss/miss/miss/wham model, but winner will probably have a few Lethal anyway from certain Merit based moves. All those knicks and light slashes that happen.<br /> <br /> In the older nWOD rules... that's not how combat usually went. Two Kung Fu Masters facing off, and whoever wins Init Whirlwind strikes the other into oblivion is not terribly epic in my book.<br /> <br /> Each is, ultimately, as boring as we choose to make it. I understand why high &quot;whiff&quot; combat can be boring because it means nothing mechanically happens most rounds which doesn't inspire lots of creative descriptions to keep it lively. But the &quot;Defense is a joke&quot; combat can be just as boring because it means most fights are over so fast nothing really got to happen besides someone unleashing massive attack on the other guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T15:07:34-07:00","id":141875,"title":"","content":"If it helps, I have a house rule I made up to help with grazing attacks. You only add a number of automatic damage equal to the dice pool used, at most. So, if you're down to 1-2 dice, you only add up to 1-2 of the weapon's damage rating. On a chance die, you don't add any automatic damage at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T17:05:14-07:00","id":141932,"title":"","con