Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> how weird. On my screen it says my post was made at 8:25 PM. I wonder why out times are an hour off. It can't be just the time zone because it's 22:59 where you are and 14:59 where I am...</div> </div> </div> </div>On Poland we have now &quot;Summer Time&quot;, so our clocks are moved on hour forward. But it's wierd that forums changes GMT timestamps with this also...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:12:06-07:00","id":142304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142130#post142130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On Poland we have now &quot;Summer Time&quot;, so our clocks are moved on hour forward. But it's wierd that forums changes GMT timestamps with this also...</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you set to local time or UTC?<br /> Again what do y'all think of keeping virtue and vice in in werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:37:44-07:00","id":142332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142304#post142304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you set to local time or UTC? Again what do y'all think of keeping virtue and vice in in werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think they should. I like the idea of each line having its own virtue/vice equivalent as well as it's own Integrity equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:08:41-07:00","id":142363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141609#post141609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that's wrong, in that GMC has and intends a very different relationship between character and player than FATE goes for.<br /> GMC has taken inspiration from FATE in some specific and small things (arguably, as I can't see into the writers' heads to see where their inspirations come from) but keeps a very different focus through all of it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.penny-arcade.com/discussion/comment/29135084/#Comment_29135084\" target=\"_blank\">This post</a> talking about GMC xp vs FATE points gives a pretty good explanation of the different goals of the systems. At no point does GMC try to go for the more 'third person view' of FATE, it firmly stays with the character.<br /> <br /> Tilts, Aspirations, etc are superficially similar, but are used to evoke a different effect within the system and interact differently with it.<br /> <br /> On a personal note, I tried FATE and intensly disliked it, but really like GMC so far. There is just no point of commonality between the two for me. Nothing in GMC evokes the FATE feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I understand what you are saying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Love FATE, and I LOVE nWOD (base). I LOVE a lot of the new Fluff, but the new mechanics just irritate me no end. I know the design space is very different between the two systems, but in the end, B&amp;S feels like an attempt to add more crunchy bits to FATE, to me. And in my opinion, Fate just does it better with less resources. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Loving the new Idigam Fluff, and am hoping to add it to my game space eventually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:12:25-07:00","id":142367,"title":"","content":"i very disliked idea of modified Virtue and Vices from <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> - to me this was only step backwards, to make game more like <b>Masquerade</b>. Werewolves shouldn't have changed V&amp;V system also because one of they greatest enemies are Bale Hounds, that are based on Seven Deadly Sins ( and two added ), and this nicely fits in to tempting character for they Vice easier path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T10:08:44-07:00","id":142447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=141800#post141800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As has been addressed, I think this is a fairly weak assessment.<br /> <br /> It also disregards that most of these things existing the nWOD previously. The Conditions/Tilts simply gather and codify lots of disparate extant things under a single (or 1.5 anyway) roof, and then tie them into the new XP mechanics. It is really hard to understand it being called &quot;clutter&quot; when it actually organizes and unifies lots of things that already existed.<br /> <br /> As well, the similarities of the Conditions and Aspects systems are very superficial. When you look at how both systems run in detail, and especially how they related to the game point economies, they differentiate heavily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them existed, but not all of them were in play as a base rule. Many of them were added with later releases from disparate expansion books (Armory Reloaded, Mirrors, Danse Macabre, etc.). Many of which we did not use at all. If it slows things down due to bookkeeping or referencing, it is Clutter. The new mechanics add clutter, no way around that really. Ironically, since those mechanics were actually designed into the FATE system as a default, and the mechanics are far less involved, they flow MUCH better in FATE than in GMC. *shrug*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that the &quot;no grazing damage without armor or Fighting Merits&quot; thing is one of the weakest aspects of the GMC combat system.<br /> <br /> Otherwise this doesn't make a lot of sense. First off, the nWOD has never been about epic combat. Either version does &quot;epic&quot; well. However... I am having trouble thinking of an &quot;epic&quot; fight involving normal (as in not supernatural) people with heavy weapons that doesn't really come down to lots of rounds of &quot;no meaningful damage done,&quot; until a big hit wins the day.<br /> <br /> <i><b>... Several epic examples... </b></i><br /> <br /> In the older nWOD rules... that's not how combat usually went. Two Kung Fu Masters facing off, and whoever wins Init Whirlwind strikes the other into oblivion is not terribly epic in my book.<br /> <br /> Each is, ultimately, as boring as we choose to make it. I understand why high &quot;whiff&quot; combat can be boring because it means nothing mechanically happens most rounds which doesn't inspire lots of creative descriptions to keep it lively. But the &quot;Defense is a joke&quot; combat can be just as boring because it means most fights are over so fast nothing really got to happen besides someone unleashing massive attack on the other guy. </div> </div> </div>Maybe &quot;Epic&quot; isn't the word that I was wanting. Lets say <i><b>Dynamic </b></i>instead. All of our combats are extremely dynamic and highly varied. Yes, sometimes they are short lived, and other times we have very involved and continuing fights. It varies. None of them are boring or simple roll fests. And again, you talk about Multi-Attacks, which we HAVE NO ISSUES with, since they are so rare in our games (1 Character actually has Combination Blow - Boxing which he has yet to use, since he far prefers fighting in his 4-legged forms where it is obviously of no use, with no other characters having multi-attacks at all) as to not really exist at all, for the most part.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it is incumbent on the GM and players to make the dice rolling something to remember rather than just rote actions. I also have not seen the &quot;Defense is a Joke&quot; issue either. Maybe we are just an odd table. I have been told that in the past. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T10:18:12-07:00","id":142456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142367#post142367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i very disliked idea of modified Virtue and Vices from <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> - to me this was only step backwards, to make game more like <b>Masquerade</b>. Werewolves shouldn't have changed V&amp;V system also because one of they greatest enemies are Bale Hounds, that are based on Seven Deadly Sins ( and two added ), and this nicely fits in to tempting character for they Vice easier path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Victorian morality is boring and tastes like cardboard. I mean, why not change the Bale Hounds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T11:35:15-07:00","id":142566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142456#post142456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Victorian morality is boring and tastes like cardboard. I mean, why not change the Bale Hounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has already changed with openness of Virtue and Vice in <b>God </b><b>Machine Chronicle</b>. In our new games I don't have Victorian-like &quot;virtues&quot; and &quot;sins&quot; in characters. Every character can pursue his own. You can, literally, make any one &quot;sin&quot; in to new Bale Hounds totem.<br /> <br /> But in <b>Blood and Smoke</b> they gone too far. Or maybe to much in backwards. Mask and Dirge was as much bad idea and soooo cWoD as it can only be. One, it is unplayable - you walk 95% of time looking as your Mask. Then only maybe in 5% of scenes you will uncover Dirge. In other game play, that is more 50-50 they become basically Virtue and Vices, that system was going to change. For me it as made only to made look <b>Requiem</b> more as <b>Masquared</b> only because the cWoD is better selling, not because Mask and Dirge system was good fitting to <b>Requiem</b>.<br /> <br /> Second, almost all nWoD supernatural are ex-mortals. Your werewolves don't go one day and say &quot;I will forget how to be a Mark I was before First Change and become living monster&quot;. If he goes this road it is still better too use extreme Harmony, not changing his &quot;Willpower regaining system&quot; into more inhuman. I could see this &quot;other Virtue and Vice&quot; system working for game like <b>Promethean</b>, when from basic, core stand being you play someone that only pretend to be human, and never was one. For werewolves - I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-19-2014, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T11:55:03-07:00","id":142589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142367#post142367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i very disliked idea of modified Virtue and Vices from <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> - to me this was only step backwards, to make game more like <b>Masquerade</b>. Werewolves shouldn't have changed V&amp;V system also because one of they greatest enemies are Bale Hounds, that are based on Seven Deadly Sins ( and two added ), and this nicely fits in to tempting character for they Vice easier path.</div> </div> </div> </div> Virtues and Vices aren't even restricted to the seven deadlies and their counterparts any more, so that feels like a very weak reason to stick to virtue and vice. There are plenty of good reasons to do so, but I don't think that's one of them. Personally, I like experimenting with different V&amp;V style mechanics. Masque and Dirge may be similar to Nature and Demeanor, but that doesn't mean they're inherently bad. I just like seeing different takes on the same basic idea of &quot;core identity trait that you use to regain willpower&quot;. That said, I can see the argument that V&amp;V works well as-is and another system might just be different but not better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T12:21:27-07:00","id":142600,"title":"","content":"I played enough CWOD and with the Nature &amp; Demeanor system to see where wyrdhamster is coming from on this. It's especially bad in LARPs, but table top suffered from the same problem. It's damn easy to play the Demeanor all the time and never let out the Nature. The Nature might be the underlying motivation, but it rarely gets stated or noticed. Virtue and Vice were a tad more obvious since one could let out the Vice for a quick fix of Willpower.<br /> <br /> Now, on the flip side, since there are<i> mechanical benefits</i> to all these things now (wasn't really in the CWOD), they might come out a lot more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:18:22-07:00","id":142713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142447#post142447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of them existed, but not all of them were in play as a base rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>So:<br /> <br /> Derangements<br /> Flaws<br /> Combat modifiers that didn't have a unified name<br /> Mundane rolls with persistent effects that were all unique.<br /> <br /> Yep, those are all in the core nWOD rule book. And they all got collapsed into the Conditions/Tilts system. That it also collapses in things like persistent supernatural effects (all in their various core books) as well only makes the point that you're making this out to be far more than it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it slows things down due to bookkeeping or referencing, it is Clutter. The new mechanics add clutter, no way around that really. </div> </div> </div>Except you're not really providing any reason to see your assessment of the new rules as extra bookkeeping or referencing. In many cases it is less because the systems have been standardized and merged.<br /> <br /> Frankly it sounds more like it slows things down for you because you don't like it, not because there's anything fundamentally wrong with the approach. The fact that you keep bringing up Fate only really reinforces my impression. The GMC rules aren't supposed to be Fate. So what Fate does is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lets say <i><b>Dynamic </b></i>instead. </div> </div> </div>Worse word. It is so subjective I have never seen it add much to an Internet discussion. It's a buzzword that ends up being used for, &quot;whatever I like.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of our combats are extremely dynamic and highly varied. </div> </div> </div>The GMC combat system is more unpredictable by having lower dice-pools. That's the math. The original rules allowed for very high combat pools which invariably lead to very predictable low variation results. The more dice being rolled, the more predictable the results, the less variation you're likely to see out of a given situation. That's why the GMC rules bring combat down to 1-4 dice attack pools. They make combat less predictable and more variable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, you talk about Multi-Attacks, which we HAVE NO ISSUES with, since they are so rare in our games (1 Character actually has Combination Blow - Boxing which he has yet to use, since he far prefers fighting in his 4-legged forms where it is obviously of no use, with no other characters having multi-attacks at all) as to not really exist at all, for the most part. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but serious Rule Zero fallacy there. &quot;The old rules are better because we didn't use the broken parts,&quot; is not convincing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Odd table&quot; or not, whatever that's really supposed to mean, you're being entirely unfair in your assessments. You're trying to make grand sweeping statements about the new rules by bringing them up in their entirety as being &quot;too much,&quot; but when you defend your preference for the old rules, you ignore all the things that are flawed in their execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:34:43-07:00","id":142725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142713#post142713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So:<br /> <br /> Derangements<br /> Flaws<br /> Combat modifiers that didn't have a unified name<br /> Mundane rolls with persistent effects that were all unique.<br /> <br /> Yep, those are all in the core nWOD rule book. And they all got collapsed into the Conditions/Tilts system. That it also collapses in things like persistent supernatural effects (all in their various core books) as well only makes the point that you're making this out to be far more than it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, if you don't have things like derangements or flaws, they mean jack squat in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except you're not really providing any reason to see your assessment of the new rules as extra bookkeeping or referencing. In many cases it is less because the systems have been standardized and merged. </div> </div> </div>Dislike is primary, and the mechanics of nWOD are FAR more complex than FATE. And since FATE does it better, why would I EVER adopt GMC?<br /> You asked me WHY I had made my choices... My feelings and desires are pretty paramount tot hat decision. SO knocking htem is pretty disingenuous, don't you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worse word. It is so subjective I have never seen it add much to an Internet discussion. It's a buzzword that ends up being used for, &quot;whatever I like.&quot;<br /> <br /> The GMC combat system is more unpredictable by having lower dice-pools. That's the math. The original rules allowed for very high combat pools which invariably lead to very predictable low variation results. The more dice being rolled, the more predictable the results, the less variation you're likely to see out of a given situation. That's why the GMC rules bring combat down to 1-4 dice attack pools. They make combat less predictable and more variable.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but serious Rule Zero fallacy there. &quot;The old rules are better because we didn't use the broken parts,&quot; is not convincing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Odd table&quot; or not, whatever that's really supposed to mean, you're being entirely unfair in your assessments. You're trying to make grand sweeping statements about the new rules by bringing them up in their entirety as being &quot;too much,&quot; but when you defend your preference for the old rules, you ignore all the things that are flawed in their execution. </div> </div> </div>Your choice to take it subjectively, not mine. You asked, I responded.<br /> <br /> And I have routinely said I hate the New Combat Mechanic... touting it does absolutely nothing for your argument. *shrug*<br /> DO YOU USE ALL THE RULES presented (I would highly doubt it, personally)? nWOD is a Tool Kit Rule System. It is my choice to use what I like and discard the rest... telling me I am doing it wrong is ludicrous in the face of that. *shrug*<br /> <br /> I don't see it as being unfair. I compare it to FATE because it is Similar to FATE. You may not like that assessment, but you cannot tell me it is wrong, because it is MY assessment, not yours. I DON'T LIKE the direction in which Crunch is moving in nWOD. That is why I will NEVER change to GMC. If I wanted to use such changes, I would use FATE (Because they work BETTER in the design space in my opinion). I don't think that nWOD is FLAWED in its execution for the base rules. It is not ignorance, it is choice to use the rules I choose and discard the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:49:14-07:00","id":142727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142713#post142713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but serious Rule Zero fallacy there. &quot;The old rules are better because we didn't use the broken parts,&quot; is not convincing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Odd table&quot; or not, whatever that's really supposed to mean, you're being entirely unfair in your assessments. You're trying to make grand sweeping statements about the new rules by bringing them up in their entirety as being &quot;too much,&quot; but when you defend your preference for the old rules, you ignore all the things that are flawed in their execution.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? He's stating his preferences and the reasons for them because he was asked to do so. If the old rules work better for his group, why on earth would they not continue to use them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T16:57:51-07:00","id":142771,"title":"","content":"Hey, so... Why the fuck are we discussing FATE vs GMC rules update appendix in the freakin' Idigam Discussion thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:02:04-07:00","id":142836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142771#post142771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, so... Why the fuck are we discussing FATE vs GMC rules update appendix in the freakin' Idigam Discussion thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cuz this is the Intrawebz <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T20:06:04-07:00","id":142981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142725#post142725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, if you don't have things like derangements or flaws, they mean jack squat in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you don't pick up the Conditions that reflect those... same thing.<br /> <br /> You not using the full base original nWOD rules does not make the GMC rules more cluttered.<br /> <br /> The only argument you can really make here is that the GMC rules put more stress on parts of the original system you didn't use. Which isn't the same thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You asked me WHY I had made my choices. </div> </div> </div>I did?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DO YOU USE ALL THE RULES presented (I would highly doubt it, personally)? nWOD is a Tool Kit Rule System. It is my choice to use what I like and discard the rest... telling me I am doing it wrong is ludicrous in the face of that. *shrug* </div> </div> </div>Nice strawman there.<br /> <br /> I neither said you have to use all the rules &quot;or you're doing it wrong,&quot; nor did I say that I use all the rules.<br /> <br /> I said that it isn't a fair comparison to say that the GMC Conditions system is too &quot;cluttered&quot; or that the new combat system is less epic/dynamic/whatever based on the fact that you weren't actually using the full system in question. You're arguing that the GMC rules need to be judged as if every rule has to be used every time, but that the older rules only need to be judged on whatever rules you felt like using.<br /> <br /> The GMC update didn't stop it from being a toolkit game. It actually added in more tool to the base-line kit (things like Down &amp; Dirty Combat and the Doors system) rather than leaving them in late supplements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may not like that assessment, but you cannot tell me it is wrong, because it is MY assessment, not yours. </div> </div> </div>Of course I can tell you that it's wrong. It being yours doesn't make it right. You can like or dislike it all you want, but that doesn't mean when you say that the GMC rules are cluttered as a matter of fact, you can most certainly be wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that nWOD is FLAWED in its execution for the base rules. </div> </div> </div>I like the pre-GMC rules just fine... but I think you're in a pretty significant minority if you actually think it managed to avoid any flaws. You might not like how the GMC went about things, but that doesn't mean there are plenty of issues with the core rules before it.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142727#post142727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the old rules work better for his group, why on earth would they not continue to use them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I say they shouldn't?<br /> <br /> I just called his reasoning into question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T20:41:08-07:00","id":142992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=142981#post142981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I say they shouldn't?<br /> <br /> I just called his reasoning into question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you play in his group I fail to see how his reasoning matters to you at all. He doesn't like the new rules. Just let him not like them, who cares if you agree with why he doesn't like them or not? Let it go and lets get back to talking about the Idigam Chronicles instead of derailing the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T21:00:06-07:00","id":143006,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I expect some thread drift but let's get the conversation back on topic guys, thanks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old