nics?<br /> <br /> Any information is read with gusto. <br /> <br /> Muchos gracias si puede ayudar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","user":"hoodedclaw","date":". 09-08-2014, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T07:20:30-07:00","id":252272,"title":"","content":"It would be awesome to hear more stories about the playtest games.<br /> <br /> Also, in line with hoodedclaw, is the Siskur Dah called upon a target when they're being a nuisance and upsetting the balance between the worlds (similar to 1e) or just...whenever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2014, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T07:35:50-07:00","id":252278,"title":"","content":"I am sure it is not smiled upon to call Siskur Dah for, say, the claiming of a large pepperoni-and-sausage pie (unless you are in a city where you are ruthlessly hunted by an overwhelming force and said pizza is the ultimate expression of your ability to survive and thrive in any circumstances) but is the Sacred Hunt a very context-specific call to action, or a philosophy the pack can apply to a wider range of goals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T07:44:17-07:00","id":252284,"title":"","content":"Siskur Dah is nothing with out proper Pack Totem - let's hear about TOTEMS! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T07:57:00-07:00","id":252314,"title":"","content":"I would love to hear about your playtest adventures, showcasing the capabilities of various pack members. On the crunchy side of things, more about Totems, Primal Urge, Siskur Dah, final versions of the forms would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T07:59:02-07:00","id":252318,"title":"","content":"What are you expecting to get spoiled, Wyrd? We already know there are new creation rules, which means we probably aren't going to find out what they are. We know they are taking a bigger part in the pack structure, but we neither know that part, specifically, or entirly how packs are going to be different... I mean, they are still writing the book. Gotta have something to sell us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T10:26:07-07:00","id":252460,"title":"","content":"Primal Urge, Lunacy, and Siskur-Dah(How exactly does that last one work?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T14:47:20-07:00","id":252676,"title":"","content":"Ok, a random discovery from my playtest game:<br /> <br /> - The Medicine skill is actually quite a useful skill still for werewolves, because of how drastically it can speed up your Aggravated damage healing times. Of course, that's only if you have some proper medical equipment - tricky to get hold of for a werewolf since, if you go into a hospital badly injured and are showing obvious rapid regeneration signs, questions will be asked. My players <i>accidentally</i> found the perfect solution. DaveB is playing the group's Bone Shadow Ithaeur. His job? He's a vet. So every so often one of the pack who gets badly mauled ends up with the indignity of being brought into the Ithaeur's veterinary practice as an injured dog, and gets medical treatment via the practice's surgery at the hands of the Ithaeur himself. DaveB's character gets to use his Medicine skill with his specialty and the benefits of his practice equipment, and it works because the werewolf is in Urshan form. No hospitals required.<br /> <br /> Of course, when it's the <i>Ithaeur</i> who gets grievously wounded, it's gonna be a bit trickier...<br /> <br /> - The pack are in the middle of a chain of spirit-bargains. They bargained with a potent spirit of abandoned dwellings (the actual name of which I will not say, as it would give away where one of the unrevealed Hunting Grounds in which we're doing our playtest is set) to help them in conflict with an enemy pack. It did so; the price of its service was that the pack had a month to empty out a nearby new house of its occupants, both spirit and flesh. The pack's elodoth set to using criminal connections to pressure the human family, but weirdly for a newbuild the garden of the house was very developed in the Shadow, <i>and</i> patrolled by a weird scythe-clawed mowing-machine spirit that looked like a hybrid scorpion of earth, vines and machinery. They decided to treat with it first rather than just hunt it down, and found that it is actually a very old harvest spirit - most recently it was the reflection of a combine-harvester until traumatic change overtook the farmland that once covered the area and repeatedly drove it into dormancy with very brief gasps of Essence. Badly weakened, in its latest cycle of awareness it managed to find a new home in the closest thing to its old reflection it could find, a new mowing machine. So now the pack are actually trying to restore it to farming machinery elsewhere in the area to try and stoke its power again and gain a new ally. To do so, they need to hunt the <i>existing</i> spirit of a combine harvester that they've identified as being appropriately resonant for the old spirit. At this point they're pretty much just going to declare Siskur-Dah on the final spirit in this chain, kill it and eat its Essence, move the old harvest spirit to the combine harvester, and get the [REDACTED] spirit into the deserted house.<br /> <br /> They already had the benefits of the [REDACTED]'s help, but they haven't turned on it because it's pretty tough (Rank 3), they want to have the possibility of future alliance with it, and the pack is half Bone Shadows.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T14:57:01-07:00","id":252679,"title":"","content":"The Siskur-Dah itself is only put in place by the Siskur-Dah rite, but a lone wolf can do the rite by themself - and it's very likely that a lone wolf will have the rite in question. You're likely to see a mixture of rites in a starting pack unless you really want to cover all the different benefits of the Sacred Hunt through different Tribal ritemasters, but the lone wolf doesn't have the luxury of friends and so I would expect would take the Sacred Hunt rite with their starting rite picks.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that werewolves don't <i>hunt</i> without the Siskur-Dah, or that those hunts can't be deeply meaningful. But the Siskur-Dah draws upon the ancient laws and pacts of the Great Wolf itself and of the Firstborn, and empowers the hunt into something more. The Warden Moon's blessing hooks into it as well, hence why the 3rd-dot Facets of the Moon Gifts draw their power through it.<br /> <br /> There are new tracking rules that look pretty nifty to me so far, although I haven't playtested them with my group yet. The tracking rules are separate from Siskur-Dah though obviously you can expect to be using them during a Sacred Hunt as a fairly likely occurrence.<br /> <br /> In theory a pack can call the Siskur-Dah for any hunt they want. They're either <i>extremely</i> devout and hold every single hunt to the utmost highest levels of dedication, or they're taking the piss. Other werewolves will judge for themselves which it is. Of course some Uratha, like say very high Primal Urge ones, are probably going to be Siskur-Dah'ing pretty regularly jfor rather different reasons.<br /> <br /> High Primal Urge werewolves have a particularly rarefied palette, you see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T15:18:13-07:00","id":252693,"title":"","content":"So no Siskur-Dah for pizza, got'cha.<br /> <br /> (I mean, I knew that already, but I was amused by the possibility.)<br /> <br /> So how about the other two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T15:42:14-07:00","id":252705,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer, wonderful teasers and all. Siskur-Dah is sort of like... Putting on your public face. Part of the enjoyment from going to a fancy restaurant is the prep, dressing up, the ambiance, the cost... It heightens the whole experience you call the hunt for and raises the stakes. Cool.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the pizza example, I love how big of a deal food during downtime is in Detroit Rock City, it was the first 'important' mundane thing that came to mind.<br /> <br /> What's the pack composition for your playthrough, auspice-wise? Anyone straining against or defying their roles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T16:10:13-07:00","id":252716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252693#post252693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no Siskur-Dah for pizza, got'cha.<br /> <br /> (I mean, I knew that already, but I was amused by the possibility.)<br /> <br /> So how about the other two?</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you like to know about Primal Urge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T16:13:33-07:00","id":252720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252705#post252705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answer, wonderful teasers and all. Siskur-Dah is sort of like... Putting on your public face. Part of the enjoyment from going to a fancy restaurant is the prep, dressing up, the ambiance, the cost... It heightens the whole experience you call the hunt for and raises the stakes. Cool.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the pizza example, I love how big of a deal food during downtime is in Detroit Rock City, it was the first 'important' mundane thing that came to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, food is somewhat of a more significant issue for werewolves now - well, largely for higher Primal Urge ones, but still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the pack composition for your playthrough, auspice-wise? Anyone straining against or defying their roles? </div> </div> </div>Bone Shadow Ithaeur, Bone Shadow Cahalith, Storm Lord Rahu, Blood Talon Irraka (killed in a fight with another pack), Iron Master Elodoth (the Irraka player's new character).<br /> <br /> Also three Wolf-Blooded who are all members of the same family as the Ithauer, a few non-Wolf-Blooded family members roughly in the know, the Ithaeur's employees at his vet practice who are sorta aware <i>something</i> goes on and keep their eyes open for certain... things they know the boss deals with, and Swift-Bloodied-Splendour, the pack's spirit totem.<br /> <br /> No-one is particularly straining against or defying their roles; we're playtesting so people wanted to stick with the kinda classic roles to see if the new rules actually work for them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T16:19:04-07:00","id":252723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252720#post252720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No-one is particularly straining against or defying their roles; we're playtesting so people wanted to stick with the kinda classic roles to see if the new rules actually work for them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As my 2 favorite Auspices are Cahalith and Elodoth (in that order), how are the playtesters enjoying their experience with those roles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T17:42:37-07:00","id":252799,"title":"","content":"<i>*wants to start sharing stories of his playtest experience, too, but isn't a writer so isn't sure if he's allowed*</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At the very least, I <i>think </i>I can say that I'm playing an Elodoth Storm Lord, and am totally foreseeing some role-defying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T17:56:08-07:00","id":252804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252720#post252720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ironically, food is somewhat of a more significant issue for werewolves now - well, largely for higher Primal Urge ones, but still.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't believe no one's asked about the food thing. Do high Primal Urge uratha only get essence from Siskur-Dah essence? Or is it like vampires, where they have to eat people? I always liked the idea of a splat that had to devour members of higher power stat to increase their own, and preyed upon members of lesser power stat as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards playing an Iron Master, a big change since due to my like of the Shadow I've always played more shaman-types and this guy's gonna be more focused on dealing with humans. I haven't figured an auspice yet, they all seem so fun now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2014, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T17:57:31-07:00","id":252806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252679#post252679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Siskur-Dah itself is only put in place by the Siskur-Dah rite, but a lone wolf can do the rite by themself - and it's very likely that a lone wolf will have the rite in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Idigam Anthology story is basically 50% this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T17:59:39-07:00","id":252808,"title":"","content":"I've really liked all the anthologies put out recently, I'm definitely looking forward to the Idigam Chronicle one the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T18:19:06-07:00","id":252829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252804#post252804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't believe no one's asked about the food thing. Do high Primal Urge uratha only get essence from Siskur-Dah essence? Or is it like vampires, where they have to eat people? I always liked the idea of a splat that had to devour members of higher power stat to increase their own, and preyed upon members of lesser power stat as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards playing an Iron Master, a big change since due to my like of the Shadow I've always played more shaman-types and this guy's gonna be more focused on dealing with humans. I haven't figured an auspice yet, they all seem so fun now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking on a way of folding this into my questions about Primal Urge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T21:14:50-07:00","id":252963,"title":"","content":"With the Bale Hounds being saved for a later release, will there at least be some mention of wounds, and how they work, and wounded spirits and whatnot? Or will all that get shunted to something later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T22:14:05-07:00","id":252990,"title":"","content":"Really wanna hear about how totems work in t his iteration of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T00:26:05-07:00","id":253105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252318#post252318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you expecting to get spoiled, Wyrd? We already know there are new creation rules, which means we probably aren't going to find out what they are. We know they are taking a bigger part in the pack structure, but we neither know that part, specifically, or entirly how packs are going to be different... I mean, they are still writing the book. Gotta have something to sell us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So I will support what <b>ArcaneArts</b> choose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252460#post252460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Urge, Lunacy, and Siskur-Dah(How exactly does that last one work?).</div> </div> </div> </div>My Primal Urge questions are those - Is Primal Urge changed in it's scope? It means something diffrent from <b>1ed</b>? Are new perks from it, beside more items you can change with? Has other drawbacks than social rolls penalty? And does high PU wolves need to eat their cousins? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other from this - any info on Lunacy would be gladly appricated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-09-2014, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T00:30:05-07:00","id":253127,"title":"","content":"Wyrd neatly said what I was going for, so yeah, that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T01:01:21-07:00","id":253146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252679#post252679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are new tracking rules that look pretty nifty to me so far, although I haven't playtested them with my group yet. The tracking rules are separate from Siskur-Dah though obviously you can expect to be using them during a Sacred Hunt as a fairly likely occurrence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've spoken to Stew about releasing the tracking rules as a spoiler, and to expand their play test circle.<br /> <br /> Hopefully soon... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T01:11:08-07:00","id":253151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252723#post252723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As my 2 favorite Auspices are Cahalith and Elodoth (in that order), how are the playtesters enjoying their experience with those roles?</div> </div> </div> </div>My group has an Elodoth Storm Lord, a Rahu Hunter in Darkness, and a Cahalith Iron Master. So far the Rahu is enjoying being terrifying without having yet entered a fight, the Elodoth pushes against both her roles by being more of an Ithaeur, and often being concerned for the welfare of her (wolf-blooded) son, exposing her weakness, and the Cahalith has found her physical and spiritual selves separated on both sides of the Gauntlet (due to a pre-game event) and is fighting in the Hisil for survival while desperately hoping her pack can retrieve her body and bring it to her. (And then hope that's enough to reunite the two sides.)<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252799#post252799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>*wants to start sharing stories of his playtest experience, too, but isn't a writer so isn't sure if he's allowed*</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At the very least, I <i>think </i>I can say that I'm playing an Elodoth Storm Lord, and am totally foreseeing some role-defying...</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's our Elodoth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T01:15:51-07:00","id":253154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252990#post252990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really wanna hear about how totems work in t his iteration of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, they're a lot more involved. The baked in assumption is that pack creation builds the Uratha, the wolf-blooded, the associated humans and builds the totem. This gives everything a sense of unity and has encouraged the players to interact with the totem.<br /> <br /> My players built themselves Wary Nest, a guardian spirit with a tendency towards overprotectiveness and fussing. They've not encountered any hostile totems yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:56:49-07:00","id":253177,"title":"","content":"I'm very glad that <b>Forsaken 2ed</b> is going with <b>Ars Magica</b>-like Troupe Playing - Uratha, Totem, Wolf-Blooded or even mortals are all part of one cohesive group.<br /> <br /> My players are all a bit disapointed now, as we hoped to get for new corebook to make changes to full <b>2ed</b>, as they are exactly in place of normal starting group - they have Totem, now are going by Rite of Initiation on next session, and they are starting to <b>think</b> as the Pack. So I was really interested <b>how</b> Totem is more <i>cohasive</i> with rest of Pack - and to be fair, how this &quot;cohesiveness&quot; is made by rules and fluff.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:52:43-07:00","id":253231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=253154#post253154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So far, they're a lot more involved. The baked in assumption is that pack creation builds the Uratha, the wolf-blooded, the associated humans and builds the totem. This gives everything a sense of unity and has encouraged the players to interact with the totem.<br /> <br /> My players built themselves Wary Nest, a guardian spirit with a tendency towards overprotectiveness and fussing. They've not encountered any hostile totems yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering what would happen if a pack picked a totem that wasn't all sharp edges and hungry gore! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> are there any pack-influences-totem or totem-influences-pack effects beyond the bans/deals the pair make with each other?<br /> <br /> Do packs' totems ever go head to head in any sort of trial or challenge, like an Urfarahmon battle? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is it possible for a pack to bind multiple (lesser?) Spirits as their totem(s)?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, NateD, yay half-moon storm lord! That's what I want to roll! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 09-09-2014, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T15:05:25-07:00","id":253618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252723#post252723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As my 2 favorite Auspices are Cahalith and Elodoth (in that order), how are the playtesters enjoying their experience with those roles?</div> </div> </div> </div>My wife, who's playing the Cahalith, says she's liked it; the Elodoth's player has only just started up the new character for a couple of sessions after his Irraka bit the dust, but seems to have plunged right in as a wheeling, dealing, networking middleman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T15:17:41-07:00","id":253627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252804#post252804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't believe no one's asked about the food thing. Do high Primal Urge uratha only get essence from Siskur-Dah essence? Or is it like vampires, where they have to eat people? I always liked the idea of a splat that had to devour members of higher power stat to increase their own, and preyed upon members of lesser power stat as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards playing an Iron Master, a big change since due to my like of the Shadow I've always played more shaman-types and this guy's gonna be more focused on dealing with humans. I haven't figured an auspice yet, they all seem so fun now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like vampires; they don't have to eat people or other werewolves. They're certainly hungry though.<br /> <br /> The old Primal Urge, where your high-PU werewolves ended up basically sleeping forever in Loci and barely able to sustain themselves outside of one due to Essence Bleed? Yeah, that's been thrown out the window.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252963#post252963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Bale Hounds being saved for a later release, will there at least be some mention of wounds, and how they work, and wounded spirits and whatnot? Or will all that get shunted to something later?</div> </div> </div> </div>Expect coverage of Wounds etc to be present but minimal in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=252990#post252990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really wanna hear about how totems work in t his iteration of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my mind, they're simpler and more effective, with much better potential to evolve over time due to the simple new way they benefit from Totem merit dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=253105#post253105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Primal Urge questions are those - Is Primal Urge changed in it's scope? It means something diffrent from <b>1ed</b>? Are new perks from it, beside more items you can change with? Has other drawbacks than social rolls penalty? And does high PU wolves need to eat their cousins? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other from this - any info on Lunacy would be gladly appricated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Primal Urge is much better now; forget items you can change with, that's not related to Primal Urge at all any more. Old Primal Urge was a stretch to justify raising for many werewolves; the new drawbacks it has are far more thematic than the old, it's far more affordable, and it's more beneficial. High-PU werewolves regenerate fast, can spend a torrent of Essence and are pretty terrifying, but they are also even deeper into the mold of the perfect hunter. I believe the phrase that came up during development was 'bodhisattva predator'.<br /> <br /> Old high-PU werewolves encouraged passivity; it encouraged the emergence of hoary old veterans that would retreat to Loci due to their Essence Bleed. New high-PU werewolves should be far more active elements of the setting. They instigate action and change. They're <i>hungry </i>predators. The Wolf Must Hunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T15:39:27-07:00","id":253638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=253627#post253627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like vampires; they don't have to eat people or other werewolves. They're certainly hungry though.<br /> <br /> The old Primal Urge, where your high-PU werewolves ended up basically sleeping forever in Loci and barely able to sustain themselves outside of one due to Essence Bleed? Yeah, that's been thrown out the window.<br /> <br /> <br /> Primal Urge is much better now; forget items you can change with, that's not related to Primal Urge at all any more. Old Primal Urge was a stretch to justify raising for many werewolves; the new drawbacks it has are far more thematic than the old, it's far more affordable, and it's more beneficial. High-PU werewolves regenerate fast, can spend a torrent of Essence and are pretty terrifying, but they are also even deeper into the mold of the perfect hunter. I believe the phrase that came up during development was 'bodhisattva predator'.<br /> <br /> Old high-PU werewolves encouraged passivity; it encouraged the emergence of hoary old veterans that would retreat to Loci due to their Essence Bleed. New high-PU werewolves should be far more active elements of the setting. They instigate action and change. They're <i>hungry </i>predators. The Wolf Must Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand they &quot;fuel&quot; the Essence each night, or something like this - and need to thirst they hunger for it. Sure, they can just hunt for spirits, but human nad werewolves are just tasty alternatives for this... Or at least I hope it's like this 'bodhisattva predator' you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:55:16-07:00","id":253675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=253231#post253231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, NateD, yay half-moon storm lord! That's what I want to roll! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I love 'em! The light and dark, and all the shades of grey in between. The constant, never-ending tight-rope walk, both internally and among the herd. The watcher at the threshold, ever-vigilant for trespass. The weight of responsibility, pulling you in every direction at once. <i>*sigh*</i><br /> <br /> Although I'm intrigued that Bunyip thinks she's a little Ithaeur-ish - that was one of my ideas, actually, or perhaps even a non-combatty Irakka. We haven't played <i>too </i>much yet, but my overall vision for her leaned more Elodoth in the end; she would be the &quot;moral compass&quot; and &quot;den mother&quot; of the pack - trying to avoid too much violence, to try to keep the others from Kuruth, and to always push for the &quot;Honourable&quot; way.<br /> <br /> We'll see how it works out, though. She also has &quot;Common Sense&quot;, but I the player am kind of getting infamous for <i>not </i>having it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=253231#post253231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any pack-influences-totem or totem-influences-pack effects beyond the bans/deals the pair make with each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Gift and a Rite that you may be interested in...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T04:50:11-07:00","id":253997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=253675#post253675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I love 'em! The light and dark, and all the shades of grey in between. The constant, never-ending tight-rope walk, both internally and among the herd. The watcher at the threshold, ever-vigilant for trespass. The weight of responsibility, pulling you in every direction at once. <i>*sigh*</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly! Having to be the impartial judge and the honorable diplomat, being strong in front of pack and spirits but approachable to the herd... Keeping your own problems together so you show no weakness while being honest as you say what you mean...<br /> <br /> Yeaaaaah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> this guy. Nate gets it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> There's a Gift and a Rite that you may be interested in...<br /> </div> </div> </div>Mmmyesss? &gt;.&gt; intrigued.<br /> <br /> I am imagining totem-building to be a mini-game, like building a mance or hallow, where you decide its strengths? I love subsystems like that. Then again, I also save-scum in Civilization 5 so I can get as many ancient ruins as possible, and let the clock run dangerously low in x-com so I can build my base just-so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T10:19:11-07:00","id":254174,"title":"","content":"So, Lunacy, how's that different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":