will forget the events they saw while under the effects of Lunacy. Willpower 5-7 requires effort on the mortal's part and an Exceptional Success to remember with perfect clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, yeah, I assumed it was all 'just' a check by roll... not likely at all but some small measure of success possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T12:51:59-07:00","id":254539,"title":"","content":"But yes, Lunacy probably causes Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T13:28:22-07:00","id":254572,"title":"","content":"Okay, so what it works like? Seeing Gauru mortal is rolling his Integrity from sheer shock, lose it, and then totally forgets about what he seen? Supernatural Fuge mechanism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T15:01:49-07:00","id":254648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=254572#post254572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so what it works like? Seeing Gauru mortal is rolling his Integrity from sheer shock, lose it, and then totally forgets about what he seen? Supernatural Fuge mechanism?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a stop-gap solution, you could have seeing a werewolf in one of the three hybrid forms be a Breaking Point against Integrity (penalty dependent on the Werewolf's form and the mortal's willpower). Success or Exceptional Success works as normal for Breaking Points, Failure or Dramatic Failure causes the False Memories Condition (from B&amp;S) and postpones Integrity loss until the character's true memories of the event are restored. When and if they remember what really happened, they lose the Integrity and gain an appropriate Condition as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T18:14:53-07:00","id":254898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=254648#post254648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a stop-gap solution, you could have seeing a werewolf in one of the three hybrid forms be a Breaking Point against Integrity (penalty dependent on the Werewolf's form and the mortal's willpower). Success or Exceptional Success works as normal for Breaking Points, Failure or Dramatic Failure causes the False Memories Condition (from B&amp;S) and postpones Integrity loss until the character's true memories of the event are restored. When and if they remember what really happened, they lose the Integrity and gain an appropriate Condition as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modifiers could also come from the circumstances surrounding the event: how clearly could the Werewolf in question be seen/heard, how long or brief was the encounter, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T22:43:20-07:00","id":255063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted 