ciation. Furthermore, to the extent that there <i>is</i> an association, you also have Wolf Gifts, which are comparatively standalone anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T16:50:37-07:00","id":260177,"title":"","content":"About Rites... Are people looking to learn them required to seek out Uratha mentors, or could they be acquired from spirits as well? This is because as far as I remember, Rites were passed down from Uratha to Uratha; this was one of the things supposed to make them special (and I thought it was a nice touch myself). Just wondering if this has changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T17:00:22-07:00","id":260180,"title":"","content":"Has there been any word on how Fetishes have been altered in the new system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T17:21:48-07:00","id":260194,"title":"","content":"So far just klaives are no longer called klaives (as it doesn't fit in with the First Tongue) and are now fetish weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T00:59:22-07:00","id":260419,"title":"","content":"Once again support the question if spirits, like Totem, for example, teach Uratha the Rites? And why Siskur-Dah is two dots one? It's a bit crucial to <b>all</b> characters in new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T02:16:40-07:00","id":260452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260419#post260419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again support the question if spirits, like Totem, for example, teach Uratha the Rites? And why Siskur-Dah is two dots one? It's a bit crucial to <b>all</b> characters in new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The volume and insistence with which we ask questions doesn't actually factor with the likelihood of them being answered. I know you're running a game, but let's try to keep spamming the questions to a minimum, shall we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T03:33:52-07:00","id":260485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260419#post260419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why Siskur-Dah is two dots one? It's a bit crucial to <b>all</b> characters in new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's more powerful and gives more than a one-dot Rite. <br /> <br /> The Siskur-dah Rite is important to characters but crucial is overstating it. Characters can live without it. They can also participate in Siskur-dah where other Uratha perform the Rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T03:52:36-07:00","id":260491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=253997#post253997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmmyesss? &gt;.&gt; intrigued.<br /> <br /> I am imagining totem-building to be a mini-game, like building a mance or hallow, where you decide its strengths? I love subsystems like that. Then again, I also save-scum in Civilization 5 so I can get as many ancient ruins as possible, and let the clock run dangerously low in x-com so I can build my base just-so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you've seen the Totemic Empowerment Rite in the Rites preview, as one of the new mechanical interactions with the totem. The other one, the Facet, is... kinda the opposite, in many ways.<br /> <br /> Totem-building isn't <i>much</i> of a mini-game; you do get to build the totem, which is a spirit, and chose what benefits you gain from it. I hope we have a chance in a future book to do a much more detailed and intricate system, but the strength of the new version compared to 1e's totem rules is that they're simpler and more easily allow for the development of the totem itself - unlike 1e where raising totem stats was painfully expensive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=254174#post254174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Lunacy, how's that different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunacy does work off Conditions, as others have suggested, and there are some Facets that let you modify the Conditions you inflict (like the Rage Facet I spoiled that allows you to apply the Berserk Condition to victims, leaving them in a furious rage with problems telling friend from foe).<br /> <br /> Lunacy also no longer works as a rough 'You must have THIS much Willpower to be a threat to a werewolf' gatekeeper that the old one did. Being strong-willed still helps, but just because you've inflicted Lunacy on humans doesn't mean they're no threat. Lunacy has more varied and interesting outcomes now. There are OTHER reasons for not going round hurling Lunacy all over the place than just 'someone might be strong-willed enough to remember what they've seen.'<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T03:59:40-07:00","id":260492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260491#post260491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you've seen the Totemic Empowerment Rite in the Rites preview, as one of the new mechanical interactions with the totem. The other one, the Facet, is... kinda the opposite, in many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Totemic abuse. Reminding those upstart spirits who's in charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T04:12:17-07:00","id":260498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=259703#post259703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As too returning to spoilers... We read about Primal Urge<i>, </i>got some answers on Lunacy, sooo...<br /> Maybe some info on Siskur-Dah? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Things we've revealed about Siskur-Dah:<br /> - It's a rite.<br /> - The original text revealed in the rites spoiler has now changed. As well as the ability to eat spirits for Essence/gain Gifts or Rites from them, there is now a specific benefit given to the pack that depends on the Tribe of the ritemaster. These specific benefits lean towards the general type of prey that the Tribe are focused on. The 'can hit ephemeral entities' is the Bone Shadow one. There are four others, one for each Forsaken Tribe.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves do not get a specific benefit. Currently I have not written up rules for the Siskur-Dah of the Pure Tribes as that's a little more involved given their different style of prey and, in particular, is <i>highly </i>relevant for the Predator Kings - something to be covered in a post-release web blog or supplement, I think.<br /> <br /> The Siskur-Dah rite applies the Sacred Hunt Condition to all participants. It's this that contains the Tribe-specific benefit, and another particular benefit as well (you can probably guess what this other benefit is).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=259783#post259783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to stay on topic and not see this turn into an image thread again, what's a Harmony 10 Primal Urge 10 Werewolf like? Being the perfect hunter doesn't help when you don't hunt and have difficulty shapeshifting at all</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I'm not sure. Maintaining Harmony 10 for any length of time as Primal Urge 10 would be really, really difficult. You'd have to be absolutely dedicated to aping humanity to an extreme, almost to a caricature, given how hard you'd have to press the breaking points towards human. You also have the fundamental problem that you can't actually get any sustenance <i>without</i> hunting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=259787#post259787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Also, recently we had a bevy of gifts spoiled. Any odds on seeing more Rites or Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Poke Stew and see if he relents <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=259852#post259852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking before, since gifts tend to be associated with certain choirs (or am I mistaken?), would it make sense for there to be sort of stand-alone gifts, similar to the goblin contracts of Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits can't bestow Gifts that aren't associated with what they represent; a spirit of bliss can't impart the Gift of Rage, for example. Wolf Gifts are 'standalone' in that they are inherent to Uratha.<br /> <br /> Because of the way Gifts interface with the spirit and Essence of the Uratha, they always come in a set of five Facets, each associated with one of the Renowns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260177#post260177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Rites... Are people looking to learn them required to seek out Uratha mentors, or could they be acquired from spirits as well? This is because as far as I remember, Rites were passed down from Uratha to Uratha; this was one of the things supposed to make them special (and I thought it was a nice touch myself). Just wondering if this has changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites can be taught by both Uratha and spirits. A lone wolf <i>can</i> acquire new rites without ever meeting another werewolf; they can travel the Shadow, hunt down spirits to demand their secrets, and observe how the laws of the Shadow interact to reveal the rites that underlie them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260180#post260180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any word on how Fetishes have been altered in the new system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the biggest change re fetishes is the role talens play.<br /> <br /> Previously, they just held the 'one-shot magic item' slot, without much guidance about what sort of power level they should have. They also lacked a good framework for their acquisition; for something so minor, you still had to fully bind spirits into talens, a significant step to take.<br /> <br /> The new talens have 1-5 dots with according effects, largely focusing on two particular types of power. You can still do the old-style random grab bag of miscellaneous stuff (like the bullets that turned into snakes) but the core talen rules have a much stronger focus on the main powerset they provide. They also offer a clearer method of getting talens (you don't need the Fetish Rite for it) that offers more interaction with the denizens of the Shadow, the politics therein, and the pack-to-pack economy of bartering fetishes, talens and favours.<br /> <br /> We offer a small number of sample fetishes and talens from 1 dot all the way to 5 dots. I'm pretty sure it's an entirely new list of items; I don't think I ended up copying any of the 1e corebook's selection.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T04:14:08-07:00","id":260499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260419#post260419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again support the question if spirits, like Totem, for example, teach Uratha the Rites? And why Siskur-Dah is two dots one? It's a bit crucial to <b>all</b> characters in new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting access to Siskur-Dah is not a significant issue in the new edition. Under 1e you could be screwed if you didn't have a member of the pack take one for the team and take Rituals dots instead of Gifts. The new edition negates this problem; not going to say how just yet but suffice to say it's an extremely simple solution <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T04:21:23-07:00","id":260504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260492#post260492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Totemic abuse. Reminding those upstart spirits who's in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. That Facet has <i>legitimate</i> use as a 'oh fuck' emergency panic button, and wonderfully bastardly use outside of that situation if you want to show your totem its place or you're just a sadist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T05:17:16-07:00","id":260531,"title":"","content":"I guess wolf gifts would explain it after all.<br /> <br /> Glad to hear talens have changed. I know WoD tries to avoid the gear-dependency of games like Dungeons and Dragons, but the way they (and fetishes) worked was always kind of weird before, considering what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T05:40:26-07:00","id":260536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260504#post260504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yes. That Facet has <i>legitimate</i> use as a 'oh fuck' emergency panic button, and wonderfully bastardly use outside of that situation if you want to show your totem its place or you're just a sadist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, totem wearing a shock collar? Nice.<br /> <br /> Do any of the tribes/auspices have a bonus to totem-wrangling? Or... No I guess that's a silly question between Bone Shadows and Elodoths, never mind. Need to think of a better question.<br /> <br /> Sorry I missed a day of checking the forum, thank ya both for the info <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am glad to hear about talens touching on the barter system, coloring pack-to-pack relations some more. I find how your pack deals with itself and other packs great rp material, obviously.<br /> <br /> How about leaving a pack? When that one big Hunt has been completed, or the one wolf that held your group together falls, or the scrappy crew that have grown into living legends find they have outgrown their alliance... I know there aren't too many stories with happy endings in WoD... Is there fallout when you unbind a totem or abandon the infrastructure you have built up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T06:32:15-07:00","id":260575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260498#post260498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, I'm not sure. Maintaining Harmony 10 for any length of time as Primal Urge 10 would be really, really difficult. You'd have to be absolutely dedicated to aping humanity to an extreme, almost to a caricature, given how hard you'd have to press the breaking points towards human. You also have the fundamental problem that you can't actually get any sustenance <i>without</i> hunting</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I'm just trying to be sneaky about spoilers since the one major reveal missing from the blog is, you know, the POWER STAT. So if a Primal Urge 10 Werewolf embodies the Hunt, what would be disadvantages for said Werewolf if they were Harmony 1? Would they even care about balancing their human side anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T08:15:54-07:00","id":260607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260498#post260498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Poke Stew and see if he relents <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I poked him. We'll see if we just poked a grumpy bear or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T08:52:20-07:00","id":260619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260607#post260607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I poked him. We'll see if we just poked a grumpy bear or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://pokethebear.50webs.org/poster4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T09:22:36-07:00","id":260654,"title":"","content":"Based on his twitter feed he seems to be in a bad mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T10:21:50-07:00","id":260734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260654#post260654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on his twitter feed he seems to be in a bad mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh oh......poor Arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T10:55:56-07:00","id":260767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260654#post260654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on his twitter feed he seems to be in a bad mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the encouragement. -_-<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm of the opinion that, no matter how pleasant, appreciative, and encouraging it might be, a request for spoilers is always annoying. You can poke a bear with a fish you intend to give it, doesn't change the fact you're poking the bear.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh shit, no wonder he's in a bad mood. I forgot about the independence vote for Scotland. I'd be pissed too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-19-2014, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T10:57:40-07:00","id":260768,"title":"","content":"Something I'm personally interested in:<br /> <br /> Is there going to be advice for running a &quot;The Days After the First Change&quot; kind of Chronicle? My players, Luna bless their hearts, are enthusiastic but Forsaken's world is just so divergent from modern pop culture werewolf myth that I know I have to do this with them baby steps. To the point where I'm calling our first Chronicle &quot;The First Season&quot; and already have all sorts of Uratha Mentors ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T11:23:08-07:00","id":260778,"title":"","content":"Might be something that comes later, most of the books kind of gloss over the moments of turning and right after, then, 'time passes' and you have all your powers and basic knowledge of the x and y splats, as well as having chosen one to join. I guess it's taken for granted you find a mentor then get set up.<br /> <br /> Do tribes try to recruit? Or do you find one that fits you? Do packs take newly changed pups under their wing? Do they bring them into the pack, or just teach them enough to send them on their way? What happens if you change in Pure territory? Or without any werewolves around? All would be good things to know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260767#post260767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the encouragement. -_-</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. Just wanted to give you a heads up. I don't know him, I just watch the Onyx Path related twitters (especially WtF2) for news on Forsaken Fridays, maybe he's the type to throw himself into games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-19-2014, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T11:27:23-07:00","id":260781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260768#post260768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'm personally interested in:<br /> <br /> Is there going to be advice for running a &quot;The Days After the First Change&quot; kind of Chronicle? My players, Luna bless their hearts, are enthusiastic but Forsaken's world is just so divergent from modern pop culture werewolf myth that I know I have to do this with them baby steps. To the point where I'm calling our first Chronicle &quot;The First Season&quot; and already have all sorts of Uratha Mentors ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of us have done this sort of thing. Start a thread on it, get a melting pot going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T09:49:03-07:00","id":261321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260499#post260499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Getting access to Siskur-Dah is not a significant issue in the new edition. Under 1e you could be screwed if you didn't have a member of the pack take one for the team and take Rituals dots instead of Gifts. The new edition negates this problem; not going to say how just yet but suffice to say it's an extremely simple solution <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh thank God for this -- I have spent entirely too much time trying to bribe and cajole someone into taking Rituals so the characters wouldn't, say, have to constantly go looking for new clothes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T18:25:59-07:00","id":261632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>underwoodfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=261321#post261321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh thank God for this -- I have spent entirely too much time trying to bribe and cajole someone into taking Rituals so the characters wouldn't, say, have to constantly go looking for new clothes.</div> </div> </div> </div>My house rule for this is if nobody wants to be a ritualist, I allow everyone to &quot;magically&quot; dedicate items to themselves at whim equal to their dots in Primal Urge. Same effect as having the ritual performed, but without the ritual portion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T06:07:29-07:00","id":262801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260531#post260531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess wolf gifts would explain it after all.<br /> <br /> Glad to hear talens have changed. I know WoD tries to avoid the gear-dependency of games like Dungeons and Dragons, but the way they (and fetishes) worked was always kind of weird before, considering what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Talens have basically been clarified and developed a bit more so that they're less of a minor side-mention and given a stronger place in the game. In terms of design space, they also <i>broadly</i> hold a different role to fetishes; it's not just that they're one-shot items, but what the one shot is <i>of</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260536#post260536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, totem wearing a shock collar? Nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nooooot exactly. I mean, you could probably do a shock collar type fetish or rite, but this Facet has a different purpose. It's just a purpose that is pretty dubious and rather open to abuse outside of that purpose <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd think of it more like forced combat drugs for your totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about leaving a pack? When that one big Hunt has been completed, or the one wolf that held your group together falls, or the scrappy crew that have grown into living legends find they have outgrown their alliance... I know there aren't too many stories with happy endings in WoD... Is there fallout when you unbind a totem or abandon the infrastructure you have built up? </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> the fallout with the totem is that the benefits it offers drop due to the lost Totem dots. As for the infrastructure, well, obviously if you leave a pack they're not likely to want to share their Loci etc with you, but I'm not sure if there is any specific mechanical impact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260575#post260575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I'm just trying to be sneaky about spoilers since the one major reveal missing from the blog is, you know, the POWER STAT. So if a Primal Urge 10 Werewolf embodies the Hunt, what would be disadvantages for said Werewolf if they were Harmony 1? Would they even care about balancing their human side anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's hard to hunt some prey when you're trapped in just one world; and low Harmony comes with its own issues around shapeshifting and other weirdness. It's also difficult to prowl amongst the herd without at least trying to mimic some of their behaviour. Being Primal Urge 10 certainly means you have a different perspective on the world as you step closer to becoming... something more, but that doesn't mean you forget everything from your life before; an Iron Master 'boddhisattva' is still an Iron Master, albeit one who really can't be passive when it comes to the hunt.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T06:18:18-07:00","id":262805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260768#post260768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'm personally interested in:<br /> <br /> Is there going to be advice for running a &quot;The Days After the First Change&quot; kind of Chronicle? My players, Luna bless their hearts, are enthusiastic but Forsaken's world is just so divergent from modern pop culture werewolf myth that I know I have to do this with them baby steps. To the point where I'm calling our first Chronicle &quot;The First Season&quot; and already have all sorts of Uratha Mentors ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to wait and see what's in the Storytelling section!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>underwoodfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=261321#post261321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh thank God for this -- I have spent entirely too much time trying to bribe and cajole someone into taking Rituals so the characters wouldn't, say, have to constantly go looking for new clothes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I really disliked the 'Rituals tax' element of the game.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons I tore out a lot of the 'admin' rites from the Rites list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T04:52:30-07:00","id":263597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=262805#post262805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one of the reasons I tore out a lot of the 'admin' rites from the Rites list.</div> </div> </div> </div>But still <i>Siskur-Dah</i> is 2nd dot Rite, even if it implemented almost <b><i>everywhere</i></b> in <b>2ed</b>, from what we see in spoilers...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wolf Must Hunt...</span><br /> <br /> But need 2nd dot in Rites to make it effectively. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T04:58:41-07:00","id":263620,"title":"","content":"Which implies you think they can't hunt effectively without that Rite. I disagree.<br /> Sacred Hunt != hunting in general","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:01:31-07:00","id":263625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=263597#post263597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But still <i>Siskur-Dah</i> is 2nd dot Rite, even if it implemented almost <b><i>everywhere</i></b> in <b>2ed</b>, from what we see in spoilers...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wolf Must Hunt...</span><br /> <br /> But need 2nd dot in Rites to make it effectively. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That contradicts everything we've heard about how the <i>Siskur-Dah Rite</i> is different from actually <i>performing</i> the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. You don't need the rite to call a Sacred Hunt, all it does is make the Sacred Hunters <i>better</i>, which when you think about it is true for <i>every </i>Rite.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What nikink said","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:13:36-07:00","id":263633,"title":"","content":"So <i>Siskur-Dah </i>( as part of Uratha culture ) is like goin on war in Middle Ages, and <i>Siskur-Dah <b>Rite</b> </i>is like blessing of priest before it that actually works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:16:50-07:00","id":263634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=263633#post263633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So <i>Siskur-Dah </i>( as part of Uratha culture ) is like goin on war in Middle Ages, and <i>Siskur-Dah <b>Rite</b> </i>is like blessing of priest before it that actually works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I hope a developer/playtester will come in and say for sure, but <b><i>from what I've seen and guessed so far </i></b>that sounds correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T17:05:11-07:00","id":264269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=262805#post262805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one of the reasons I tore out a lot of the 'admin' rites from the Rites list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides Rite of Dedication, what other rites did you feel were &quot;admin&quot; rites? My guess would be Sacred Hunt, Rite of Healing, and Bind Spirit<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T18:37:58-07:00","id":264311,"title":"","content":"The rites that come to my mind are things like Funeral Rite, Rite of the Spirit Brand, Rite of Initiation, Rite of Renunciation, and Rite of Contrition. They're things that are required to keep the bureaucracy of Uratha/Spirit relations going, but they don't really do anything that makes it feel like you aren't just paying an XP tax in order to be able to do the basic job of a ritemaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T00:32:58-07:00","id":264434,"title":"","content":"I think the confusion comes from misusing terminology. True, we've said many times 'The Wolf Must Hunt'. What we haven't said is 'The Wolf Must Siskur-dah'.<br /> <br /> Siskur-dah literally means 'sacred hunt' (if I remember the First Tongue correctly). The Siskur-dah is special. The Uratha perform the Rite and hunt something specific based on that Rite, and the ritemaster's tribe. They gain specific advantages from doing so. If they don't perform the Siskur-dah Rite, they're not doing a Siskur-dah, they're just hunting. That's fine, hunting is what werewolves do. The Wolf Must Hunt, after all.<br /> <br /> The typical pack will have many, many hunts, and most of them won't be Siskur-dah. Again, the Siskur-dah is special. It is for calling out a specific prey and marking that thing to die. It is claiming <u>that</u> prey for <u>this</u> pack and receiving spiritual endorsement to make it so. Calling a Siskur-dah for every hunt would feel wrong to the average wolf. It would profane the sacred and belittle what makes them apex predators.<br /> <br /> They also can't call a Siskur-dah for every hunt. They have limits, so they need to choose when the hunt needs to be made sacred.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as I recall, there's no penalty for not engaging in Siskur-dah. An Uratha can live her whole life without performing or participating in the sacred hunt and she won't suffer - except maybe losing social status if the other wolves in her area consider it a sign of weakness or whatever.<br /> <br /> So wyrdhamster's quote 'So <i>Siskur-Dah </i>( as part of Uratha culture ) is like goin on war in Middle Ages, and <i>Siskur-Dah <b>Rite</b> </i>is like blessing of priest before it that actually works?' needs tweaking because there is no Siskur-dah part of Uratha culture without the Rite. There is the hunt, and The Wolf Must Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T01:00:17-07:00","id":264439,"title":"","content":"So if <i>Siskur-dah</i> is talked in detail - could we see more info on Primal Urge? We know it's make you &quot;bodhisattva predator&quot; in the end, but what things it's affect? What are perks of higher than PU 1 in <b>Forsaken 2ed</b>? Will joining Lodges been based on this, like adding Bloodline to the Kindred is in <b>Requiem</b>, or like Legacies are connected to Gnosis in <b>Awakening</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T01:20:35-07:00","id":264446,"title":"","content":"You're like a bloodhound on a scent, wyrdhamster. Much like in 1st edition, as Primal Urge increases, it improves some of the Uratha's abilities and imposes other limitations and complications.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not going to say what changes and by how much. I'm happy to talk about how elements impact the setting in broad terms, but I'm not going to cut and paste tables with numbers onto this forum. If Stew wants to do that, he's the developer and he can. As writers, we can't be specific without permission, because NDAs. You'll just have to wait for the book to get that level of detail, sorry.<br /> <br /> We don't have all the specific details on Lodges yet. As pure speculation on my part, I'd imagine that different Lodges would have different entry requirements. Some may be based on PU, others may not. Stew and I have spoken about releasing a web enhancement after 2nd edition is released that details the Dreaming Lodge from Red Centre - that might be where we start to clarify how Lodge entry requirements work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T01:32:44-07:00","id":264450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264269#post264269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Rite of Dedication, what other rites did you feel were &quot;admin&quot; rites? My guess would be Sacred Hunt, Rite of Healing, and Bind Spirit</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacred Hunt = Siskur-Dah;<br /> Bind Spirit and Healing Rite? Nope. Not 'admin rites' at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T02:08:47-07:00","id":264457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264446#post264446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm not going to say what changes and by how much. I'm happy to talk about how elements impact the setting in broad terms, but I'm not going to cut and paste tables with numbers onto this forum. If Stew wants to do that, he's the developer and he can. As writers, we can't be specific without permission, because NDAs. You'll just have to wait for the book to get that level of detail, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking about it. Rather what can change in story terms - you say that more PU means that Uratha is more like bloodhound, So I can assume that, for example, Perception mechanics can be amplifyed by your PU? That more &quot;wolf&quot; Uratha are really more superb hunters? Fresh after First Change cub can find his lover, but old hounds - with high PU -can easily discern relatives of they enemies, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T02:30:06-07:00","id":264465,"title":"","content":"No, I said you are like a bloodhound - one sniff of an answer about something else and you're back in with PU questions. Not that Uratha are like bloodhounds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T04:36:28-07:00","id":264499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=263597#post263597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But still <i>Siskur-Dah</i> is 2nd dot Rite, even if it implemented almost <b><i>everywhere</i></b> in <b>2ed</b>, from what we see in spoilers...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wolf Must Hunt...</span><br /> <br /> But need 2nd dot in Rites to make it effectively. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Getting access to the Siskur-Dah rite is not a significant problem unless you choose it to be - that's all I can say at this stage without going into details that you'll probably have to wait for the book to see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264269#post264269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Rite of Dedication, what other rites did you feel were &quot;admin&quot; rites? My guess would be Sacred Hunt, Rite of Healing, and Bind Spirit</div> </div> </div> </div>Things like Funeral, Contrition, Renunciation - Rites that don't do anything mechanical at all and take up word-count, things that should really be roleplay rather than stuff you have to spend Experience on but yet somehow you can't do without buying them. They're still ritualised parts of werewolf society, but they're not <i>Rites</i> - they're not exploiting ancient pacts or the laws of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Actually fucking about with binding spirits and making them do what you want, that sort of thing is still Rite material. The aim now is that all the Rites <i>do</i> something meaningful and mechanical. I didn't have a huge amount of word-count to cram my vision of Rites into, so everything that went in had to have impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T04:52:53-07:00","id":264524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264311#post264311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rites that come to my mind are things like Funeral Rite, Rite of the Spirit Brand, Rite of Initiation, Rite of Renunciation, and Rite of Contrition. They're things that are required to keep the bureaucracy of Uratha/Spirit relations going, but they don't really do anything that makes it feel like you aren't just paying an XP tax in order to be able to do the basic job of a ritemaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely that.<br /> <br /> You should see the Rites and <i>want</i> your character to buy them, not have the group sighing and wondering who is going to shoulder the burden of the Spirit Brand XP tax. Being a ritemaster should mean having significant power over the Shadow and the world in a different manner to Gifts, and every Rite you pick should be as appealing and give a sense of expanding ritual knowledge and mastery. Werewolves who don't choose Rites as their main focus should still find that Rites are cool enough that they want to ensure they have a few for teamwork with the primary ritemasters in the group.<br /> <br /> The Rite of the Sacred Hunt may be the closest thing to an 'Experience tax' in the new Rites but it has serious benefits, and also invokes the ancient power of the Great Predator itself - a genuinely sacred act for the Wolf's Children. Mechanically, it also encourages there being more than one dedicated ritualist in a group, since each Tribe has different benefits from the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> I remember one Werewolf game where we had the Cahalith become a secondary ritualist - the Ithaeur was, of course, the primary one. It was a bit of a slog for both of them. With the Rituals discount, the Ithaeur 'had' to be the main ritualist and had to sweep up all sorts of admin rites. The Cahalith, meanwhile, was always very much second-string - she had to sink even more XP into Rituals dots than the Ithaeur so that she could access the rites she wanted.<br /> <br /> In 2e, the Ithaeur no longer has a swathe of admin Rites; every Rite he or she picks significantly bulks out his or her armoury of shamanic power. The Ithaeur is also no longer pidgeonholed to being the group ritemaster; <i>anyone</i> can do that, there are no Rituals dots to buy first to unlock access to Rites and the Ithaeur receives no discounts. The Cahalith, or anyone who has the Experiences, can go 'I want <i>that</i> Rite' and they won't have to hit the 'You must be THIS tall' gatekeeping of Rituals dots. Being a dabbler is totally valid, and will still add meaningful oomph to the pack's capabilities. The only limitation on Rites access, as long as you have the Experiences, is that you need to find someone or something that you can learn the ritual symbolism from. In most cases, that's easy. In a few cases, the secrets are guarded rather more closely...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T05:04:26-07:00","id":264528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264446#post264446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're like a bloodhound on a scent, wyrdhamster. Much like in 1st edition, as Primal Urge increases, it improves some of the Uratha's abilities and imposes other limitations and complications.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not going to say what changes and by how much. I'm happy to talk about how elements impact the setting in broad terms, but I'm not going to cut and paste tables with numbers onto this forum. If Stew wants to do that, he's the developer and he can. As writers, we can't be specific without permission, because NDAs. You'll just have to wait for the book to get that level of detail, sorry.<br /> <br /> We don't have all the specific details on Lodges yet. As pure speculation on my part, I'd imagine that different Lodges would have different entry requirements. Some may be based on PU, others may not. Stew and I have spoken about releasing a web enhancement after 2nd edition is released that details the Dreaming Lodge from Red Centre - that might be where we start to clarify how Lodge entry requirements work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd quite like to work up the Lodge of the [REDACTED] from my [REDACTED] Hunting Ground as a full write-up, as well as maybe the Lodge of [REDACTED] mentioned in a sidebar in the Idigam section if that survives the word-count cull into the final book.<br /> <br /> To be honest, there's a ton of stuff I want to do that we just don't have space for in the book, but whether it turns up in web enhancements kinda also depends on when topics are scheduled further down the line (I'd like to do the Pure Gifts and the Sacred Hunt tribal benefits for the Pure, but I have no idea when the Pure will be covered in the actual supplements).<br /> <br /> Also, putting REDACTED in posts is quite fun, hopefully it wasn't so oblique that Bunyip couldn't figure out which Lodges I meant <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T05:19:35-07:00","id":264537,"title":"","content":"Not at all. I very much want you to write those lodges too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For everyone else out there, I know the process takes longer than anyone wants, but I hope you love the final product as much as we've loved writing it. The sheer creativity, energy and enthusiasm of the writing team has been fantastic to work with - the number of extras we all want to write to expand the world is proof to me how much we want the book to be in your hands, to talk openly about it with you and come up with new ideas and stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T05:51:53-07:00","id":264552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264446#post264446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If Stew wants to do that, he's the developer and he can. As writers, we can't be specific without permission, because NDAs. You'll just have to wait for the book to get that level of detail, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe ask Stew about proper spoiler on Primal Urge ( or other topic )? It was <i>weeks</i> from last one, there are about <b>4 months</b> ( at least ) of waiting more in line - some raw meat would be great for us, fans, to talk about in light of <b>Forsaken 2ed</b>.<br /> <br /> Once I said - I would just love to see how PU was tweaked in general, story implications terms, no mechanics is need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-24-2014, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T07:01:07-07:00","id":264581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=260452#post260452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The volume and insistence with which we ask questions doesn't actually factor with the likelihood of them being answered. I know you're running a game, but let's try to keep spamming the questions to a minimum, shall we?</div> </div> </div> </div>This bears being repeated I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T07:36:56-07:00","id":264601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264552#post264552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe ask Stew about proper spoiler on Primal Urge ( or other topic )? It was <i>weeks</i> from last one, there are about <b>4 months</b> ( at least ) of waiting more in line - some raw meat would be great for us, fans, to talk about in light of <b>Forsaken 2ed</b>.<br /> <br /> Once I said - I would just love to see how PU was tweaked in general, story implications terms, no mechanics is need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, I already poked Stew. Let's not poke the raven too much lest he eat our livers straight from our bodies.<br /> <br /> I've asked, all we can do is wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-24-2014, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T08:42:36-07:00","id":264627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264552#post264552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe ask Stew about proper spoiler on Primal Urge ( or other topic )? It was <i>weeks</i> from last one, there are about <b>4 months</b> ( at least ) of waiting more in line - some raw meat would be great for us, fans, to talk about in light of <b>Forsaken 2ed</b>.<br /> <br /> Once I said - I would just love to see how PU was tweaked in general, story implications terms, no mechanics is need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things about Primal Urge that I've already mentioned, condensed here:<br /> - It's far better value than in 1e.<br /> - Increasing your Primal Urge means you can spend more Essence and regenerate faster. Expect a superior rate of increased Essence per turn compared to 1e; look more to the later games and B&amp;S for the sort of rates involved.<br /> - The old Primal Urge drawbacks basically encouraged passivity - at high levels, you ended up unable to interact effectively with humans and with a strong incentive to sleep on a Locus and not leave it much. The new drawbacks encourage the opposite - activity.<br /> - The story implication of this is that high Primal Urge Uratha are no longer hoary old veterans that you seek out because they might know something you need or because you need their help with something specific - instead, they're story <i>drivers</i>. A high Primal Urge Uratha is an instigator, a paragon of the hunt and thus a creature that <i>does</i> hunt rather than sleeping in a magic cave somewhere.<br /> <br /> This has all already been mentioned here and elsewhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We can't really give you more than this, as it involves getting into the details of the mechanics to explain things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T11:15:30-07:00","id":264686,"title":"","content":"At the risk of sounding like a pest, I'm salivating over this book to be released and I just have one question regarding potential wait time....Are we looking at something closer to Halloween or closer to Christmas as far as a potential -general- time of release? I only ask cause it seems like the developing and writing seems to be done. At least that's what I'm gathering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T11:27:53-07:00","id":264696,"title":"","content":"I personally doubt it, but a friend of mine did bring up an interesting question. The previous iterations of 2e both have rules for membership in multiple factions, with Demons having a merit that let's them be in two Agendas and Vampires having a sort of social status cap that let's them mingle in different Covenants. Will anything remotely like this be in Forsaken 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T12:59:49-07:00","id":264749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264627#post264627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Things about Primal Urge that I've already mentioned, condensed here:<br /> - It's far better value than in 1e.<br /> - Increasing your Primal Urge means you can spend more Essence and regenerate faster. Expect a superior rate of increased Essence per turn compared to 1e; look more to the later games and B&amp;S for the sort of rates involved.<br /> - The old Primal Urge drawbacks basically encouraged passivity - at high levels, you ended up unable to interact effectively with humans and with a strong incentive to sleep on a Locus and not leave it much. The new drawbacks encourage the opposite - activity.<br /> - The story implication of this is that high Primal Urge Uratha are no longer hoary old veterans that you seek out because they might know something you need or because you need their help with something specific - instead, they're story <i>drivers</i>. A high Primal Urge Uratha is an instigator, a paragon of the hunt and thus a creature that <i>does</i> hunt rather than sleeping in a magic cave somewhere.<br /> <br /> This has all already been mentioned here and elsewhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We can't really give you more than this, as it involves getting into the details of the mechanics to explain things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry for sounding a bit nerd raging (?) but...<br /> <br /> Fan Must Hunt! ( The spoilers until the release date <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> This change in perspectvie on Primal Urge is very plusable - I always was a bit wierd you make more &quot;wolfish&quot; Uratha to be immobile statues in Shadow. Pitty rest of changes can't be shown because of NDA, but at least we know that now old and might Uratha are really leading the Hunts, and don't wait &quot;in huts&quot; fr cubs to bringe them Essence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T05:38:01-07:00","id":265359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264686#post264686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of sounding like a pest, I'm salivating over this book to be released and I just have one question regarding potential wait time....Are we looking at something closer to Halloween or closer to Christmas as far as a potential -general- time of release? I only ask cause it seems like the developing and writing seems to be done. At least that's what I'm gathering.</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea, sorry. That's the arena of people higher up the Onyx chain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264696#post264696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally doubt it, but a friend of mine did bring up an interesting question. The previous iterations of 2e both have rules for membership in multiple factions, with Demons having a merit that let's them be in two Agendas and Vampires having a sort of social status cap that let's them mingle in different Covenants. Will anything remotely like this be in Forsaken 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so; Tribes are not like Covenants. They feature a bond to a totemic wolf-god rather than just being social apparati. I could be wrong though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=264749#post264749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for sounding a bit nerd raging (?) but...<br /> <br /> Fan Must Hunt! ( The spoilers until the release date <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> This change in perspectvie on Primal Urge is very plusable - I always was a bit wierd you make more &quot;wolfish&quot; Uratha to be immobile statues in Shadow. Pitty rest of changes can't be shown because of NDA, but at least we know that now old and might Uratha are really leading the Hunts, and don't wait &quot;in huts&quot; fr cubs to bringe them Essence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Primal Urge was one of the problematic bits of 1e that we honed in on fairly rapidly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:06:13-07:00","id":265475,"title":"","content":"Any good playtest stories recently, Acrozatatim? Its been a couple weeks, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:10:40-07:00","id":265478,"title":"","content":"Relevant to this thread, posted elsewhere:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265445#post265445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Hisil in second edition...<br /> <br /> * I describe the inside of the Gauntlet. In 1e you stood in one world for the time it took to cross, then crossed. Now, you vanish from one world, hang inside the Gauntlet for a few Turns and then appear on the other side. Sometimes, you see things in there.<br /> <br /> * We've given Helios a purpose and motivation other than just &quot;Luna's twin brother,&quot; which doesn't alter how Helions act toward werewolves but reveals much about the Hisil's &quot;physics&quot;<br /> <br /> * A lot of attention is placed on describing what the Shadow looks, feels, and tastes like - it's a sensory experience, especially for an Uratha.<br /> <br /> * Werewolve's Essence-senses are explicitly perceived as their sense of smell/taste. You don't *see* dormant spirits, you taste them in the not-air.<br /> <br /> * One of the example spirits is a big-box retailer; they act like corpulent slum-lords of the Shadow, enslaving the lesser spirits linked to the goods and consumers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>VERY MUCH </b>LIKE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:13:28-07:00","id":265479,"title":"","content":"I should probably know this already, but I take it there's a difference between the Gauntlet and Twilight? I didn't figure that there was much to the Gauntlet other than it being a barrier between the Shadow and the Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:19:32-07:00","id":265482,"title":"","content":"The Gauntlet was just a barrier, with no relation to the Twilight.<br /> <br /> I still don't think it does have a relation to the Twilight, but the impression I get is that it's now more of a gaping wound-canyon between worlds. That impression isn't based on anything said, it's just a cool image that fits the idea of seeing things in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:23:21-07:00","id":265485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=265475#post265475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any good playtest stories recently, Acrozatatim? Its been a couple weeks, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>DaveB has been somewhat inconvenienced so we haven't managed to get together for Werewolf these last two weeks; plus we're moving on to Mage playtesting soon. Still, I'm hoping we get to have our final session featuring a Siskur-Dah against a combine harvester, I kid you not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:32:38-07:00","id":265489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=265485#post265485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DaveB has been somewhat inconvenienced so we haven't managed to get together for Werewolf these last two weeks; plus we're moving on to Mage playtesting soon. Still, I'm hoping we get to have our final session featuring a Siskur-Dah against a combine harvester, I kid you not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having Alan Wake flashbacks.<br /> <br /> Do try and have that hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:43:19-07:00","id":265493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=265479#post265479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should probably know this already, but I take it there's a difference between the Gauntlet and Twilight? I didn't figure that there was much to the Gauntlet other than it being a barrier between the Shadow and the Flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight is the immaterial state of being an ephemeral being has while in the plain, vanilla, mortal, solid world.<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet is the in-between place that's not the solid world and not the shadow world. Formerly, it was just a barrier. Now, it looks like it's being expanded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:47:46-07:00","id":265497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=265493#post265493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilight is the immaterial state of being an ephemeral being has while in the plain, vanilla, mortal, solid world.<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet is the in-between place that's not the solid world and not the shadow world. Formerly, it was just a barrier. Now, it looks like it's being expanded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, cool. I'm not 100% on how the Shadow works in 1E (<b>Lore of the Forsaken</b>, arriving soon, should fix that), so I didn't know if hanging out &quot;In the Gauntlet&quot; was a thing I should have known about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avata