:"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T02:52:23-07:00","id":266069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266061#post266061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forgive you for not officially announcing Bale Hounds book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know I may act like Shricking Geek, but it's only because I'm newly converted <b>Forsaken 2ed</b> fan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Even if I disliked 1ed )</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't announce something I don't know exists. I mean, I <i>could, </i>but I fail to see how that's useful.<br /> <br /> And I dig it, because <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken </b>has been my favorite game line of the nWoD since before it came out. It truly was a labor of love to work on the new core, and if I get to work on any future supplements if we have them, that'll just be icing on an already awesome cake.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T03:26:42-07:00","id":266073,"title":"","content":"I just wanna see the current lodge template so I can start to write my Elementalist lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T03:39:07-07:00","id":266075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266073#post266073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanna see the current lodge template so I can start to write my Elementalist lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the concept behind this Elementalist lodge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T04:54:27-07:00","id":266086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266075#post266075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the concept behind this Elementalist lodge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Five young Uratha were given five special rings. When their talens combine, their totem becomes Captain Planet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T06:05:11-07:00","id":266111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266086#post266086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Five young Uratha were given five special rings. When their talens combine, their totem becomes Captain Planet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally there's a corresponding Pure Lodge dedicated to Captain Pollution. Or I guess another Forsaken Lodge. That way I could join <i>them</i> and finally fulfill my dream of killing Captain Planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T06:21:20-07:00","id":266117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266075#post266075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the concept behind this Elementalist lodge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Re-purposed Lodge of Seasons, each Season tied with a corresponding element. The Uratha would regard his chosen Season as affinity renown. Summer = Glory; Autumn = Wisdom; Winter = Cunning and Spring = Honor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T08:24:30-07:00","id":266171,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Gauntlet and the Hisil, is there going to be at least a concrete representation on harvesting essence from Loci or places of intense emotion? The Territories book makes mention of this but I've struggled to find a concrete write-up that says &quot;This is how it's done&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T08:56:46-07:00","id":266196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266171#post266171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Gauntlet and the Hisil, is there going to be at least a concrete representation on harvesting essence from Loci or places of intense emotion? The Territories book makes mention of this but I've struggled to find a concrete write-up that says &quot;This is how it's done&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about techniques for maintaining it, keeping it going, etc.<br /> <br /> Or just how an Uratha takes Essence from it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: the Forsaken corebook, page 263</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To draw Essence from a locus, a werewolf must be<br /> in contact with the locus\u2019 physical form, either in the<br /> physical world or in the Shadow. The player then rolls<br /> Harmony; the werewolf may take up to one Essence point<br /> per success from the locus\u2019 reserve. It takes one minute for<br /> each point of Essence to transfer.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T11:36:10-07:00","id":266321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266086#post266086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Five young Uratha were given five special rings. When their talens combine, their totem becomes Captain Planet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately: &quot;But everything changed when the Fire Lodge attacked!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T12:11:26-07:00","id":266362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=266321#post266321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternately: &quot;But everything changed when the Fire Lodge attacked!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god, Captain Planet was the first Avatar.<br /> <br /> Nevermind what Korra says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T13:09:10-07:00","id":266391,"title":"","content":"I am frantically trying to think of another elementally motif'd cultural touchstone to urathize.<br /> <br /> A Werewolf: the Gathering collectable trading card game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T13:58:32-07:00","id":266403,"title":"","content":"The Fantastic Furry Four? Mister Fantasic = Water. Invisible Woman = Air. Human Torch = Fire. Thing = Earth<br /> <br /> The Fifth Element - self explanatory","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T07:17:45-07:00","id":270110,"title":"","content":"So, some questions for you all. What do you like or dislike about the existing Lodges, the way they're set up and structured? What are your favourite Lodges, and why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:21:52-07:00","id":270136,"title":"","content":"Lodge of Night. Cuz they like supernatural arabic ninja andcus its sumple-character was really bad-ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:57:36-07:00","id":270155,"title":"","content":"Let's see... Generally, Lodge prerequisites are stringent compared with any boons they may provide, excluding specific fetishes, which more often than not have no raison d'etre to be so exclusive to begin with. Fashion statements about their spirit bound tools are fine. Exclusive rites are fine too.<br /> <br /> But when we get to lodges and see things like &quot;Oh this one gives a gift list as affinity and a +1 for this roll. Oh look at this one. It makes every Mental Skill cost like merits, THAT'S AMAZING!&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is why I'd like for specific tribal lodges to afford other renowns at affinity costs, for example. Blood Talon Lodge that puts the dead to rest? give 'em Wisdom cookies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T09:37:05-07:00","id":270169,"title":"","content":"A more standarized way to adjudicate requisites and benefits to create your own would be lots of good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T10:32:18-07:00","id":270193,"title":"","content":"Since lodges seem to be so specific, a disclaimer or sidebar reminding players that they can 'soften' things - or maybe guidelines for writing up a lodge of your own so the ST feels more comfortable rewarding players with the opportunity to engage them? Probably not the sort of thing that you have room for in the core book, but I have operated under the impression that 'prestige classes' in NWoD are a bit... Extraneous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T13:21:13-07:00","id":270318,"title":"","content":"BTW, will Idigam Chronicles be finished ANYWHEN?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T13:47:37-07:00","id":270339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=270318#post270318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, will Idigam Chronicles be finished ANYWHEN?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a side discussion. It's not for the core book - our drafts for that are done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T13:48:46-07:00","id":270340,"title":"","content":"It will be ready when its ready. Maybe early first half of 2015.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T14:40:08-07:00","id":270365,"title":"","content":"I think I have a favourite Lodge for every Tribe, actually. In no particular order:<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Masters:</b> Lodge of Lightning. I like determination, and I like cleverness. These guys take the best traits of Iron Masters and Storm Lords and fuse into one. I am unable to dislike that combination. <br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons:</b> Lodge of Garm. Where the Lightning Dancers branched out from their main path, these guys turned inwards, and focused even more on the warrior ideal. I also like the Norse symbolism, because, hey, fan of that.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords: </b>Lodge of Winter. Wise rulers. Similar to the Iron Master example, this is a good fusion between two tribe mentalities. Storm Lords on one hand, and Bone shadows on the other. I also really like the &quot;Pillars of the Storm&quot; concept, of having the tribe core basically being one of the three pillar-lodges.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadows: </b>Lodge of Death. No question here. Mystic werewolf-necromancers of the old school? With lots of dark lore and secrets? Simply great. I especially like the little hints that they don't have a full spirit as lodge totem, but something else, something that allows them to travel through the Underworld without the normal problems werewolves have. A Geist perhaps? Hmm. Mystery indeed. (Or was that just the Pickering pack? Ah well, Lodge of Death mysteries anyhow.)<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters in Darkness: </b>Lodge of Harmony. This one was harder for me, since they are the only Tribe I haven't used extensively. But the theme of purification and warding they have is something I really like.<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, I like the Lodges, they are nice little niches inside the Tribes. When I first thought about it, my initial reaction was that they were good, but many of them were... restraining in what kind of character could join, or in the actions they'd have to take. But as I glanced through the Lodge books I realized that wasn't the case, and those that required that much dedication were a minority. <br /> All in all, I like them because they are yet another way of defining character.<br /> <br /> What I don't like about them, however, is the benefits. It's not just that they are often quite weak, they are extremely inconsistent as well. Lodge of Death count their Harmony as 2 higher to resist Death Rage, while Lodge of Night gets XP cost reduction, night vision, and an ability to ignore 1 Defence, or that the Lodge of Doors get a completely unique Gift List.<br /> <br /> I don't need them to be either strong or weak, but at least make most of them consistent. I don't want my players to think &quot;Hmm, this fits my character better, but the benefits of that lodge are simply too good to pass up.&quot; It's ok if a few, like Lodge of Scars, are special, because they are, but most of them should be at least approximately the same.<br /> <br /> It would also be nice if Lodges were something one could come and go from. Perhaps be a member of them for a few years, but then when one has changed as a person, it'd be ok to leave, perhaps to found a lodge of your own, or join another that fits who you've become more. It would also make it contrast nicely with Legacies and Bloodlines. <br /> <br /> And that said, Rant over. Hope this was the kind of thing you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T14:54:20-07:00","id":270416,"title":"","content":"I don't have many gripes with Lodges as a whole but my biggest complaint is with the Lodge of Lightning...It was described 3 different ways in 3 different books. Lore of the Forsaken mentioned it as a high tech lodge making high tech weapons and equipment for the Tribe, the Lodge book described it as Hardcore wolves who throw themselves at their goals, going a 100 mph straight ahead until the task was done, and the Core book described it a different way...I'd just like consistency between all the books when they hint at Lodges...and yes, maybe some improved/ more thematically appropriate benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T15:27:08-07:00","id":270423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=270416#post270416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have many gripes with Lodges as a whole but my biggest complaint is with the Lodge of Lightning...It was described 3 different ways in 3 different books. Lore of the Forsaken mentioned it as a high tech lodge making high tech weapons and equipment for the Tribe, the Lodge book described it as Hardcore wolves who throw themselves at their goals, going a 100 mph straight ahead until the task was done, and the Core book described it a different way...I'd just like consistency between all the books when they hint at Lodges...and yes, maybe some improved/ more thematically appropriate benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't know that they were in Lore, but they are pretty much the same in Lodges: The Faithful and the core book. Sure, they have differences, but small enough that they can be attributed to differing viewpoints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T16:13:16-07:00","id":270462,"title":"","content":"Lodge of Death, and anything that has to do with the Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T17:40:40-07:00","id":270511,"title":"","content":"One thing that I don't like, is that the lodges are exclusive to particular tribes. Some of the lodges seem like they fit pretty well in a couple of tribes, biggest example for me is the lodge of the shield, which works great from the blood talon perspective as a warrior who protects his people and is a part of a martial brotherhood, but it also works from an iron master perspective as being a member of the community, helping werewolves to blend in with the herd, and particularly, with hunting humans. I could even see stormlords joining the lodge coming from an angle of &quot;community policing&quot; in which they act as a role model to their community by conducting themselves in a manner befitting an officer and ensuring social order through both example and enforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T18:09:47-07:00","id":270517,"title":"","content":"Three big things I like about lodges. The first is when they offer a motivation for a character that can conceivably put them at odds with the rest of their pack. They want to hunt a prey the others don't see an issue with, they want to explore something the others might think is too dangerous, they believe in something that the others find disagreeable. The other (this isn't with all the lodges) is that they offer a totem that, while not as close to heart as a pack totem, is often far more close to the werewolf than Luna or their tribal totem. They speak with the members of their lodge. This can help with my first like, since everyone in the pack is involved with their totem, but the lodge member is involved with them and this other one. And lastly, I like how there are kind of two types of lodges, the public ones where you may not advertise yourself but people know of the lodges and might seek you out for it, or the shadow lodges, where you're the member of a sort of secret cabal that few people know exist, let alone able to recognize that you're part of it.<br /> <br /> I like a lot of lodges, some that stand out are the Lodge of Mania and Wires, the Hidden Hunt and Maelstrom, Shadow Throne and Spirit Chains, Storms Eye and Cerberus. The Pure lodges seem very cool, I've always liked the Lodges of Fevered Light and Night's Fear. I have to agree with some that the benefits can seem to vary too much from lodge to lodge. But the only thing I really don't like about some lodges is their hyper-specialization, so to speak. Something like the Lodge of the Shield, which exists solely for the werewolf members of the LAPD as a sort of support group to help cover each others backs. It's a valid idea, I guess, but seems like the kind of thing that could be wrapped up in a paragraph suggesting that it's a phenomenon common to werewolves in law enforcement all over, rather than just in this one city, and it seems more like a sort of common sense thing rather than something that might require a spiritual totem. A few other lodges have that problem, like the lodge of Silence and the Lodge of the Lake, which seems more like a large pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T20:07:59-07:00","id":270542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=270511#post270511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I don't like, is that the lodges are exclusive to particular tribes. Some of the lodges seem like they fit pretty well in a couple of tribes, biggest example for me is the lodge of the shield, which works great from the blood talon perspective as a warrior who protects his people and is a part of a martial brotherhood, but it also works from an iron master perspective as being a member of the community, helping werewolves to blend in with the herd, and particularly, with hunting humans. I could even see stormlords joining the lodge coming from an angle of &quot;community policing&quot; in which they act as a role model to their community by conducting themselves in a manner befitting an officer and ensuring social order through both example and enforcement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dunno, some, such as the Pillars of the Storm-Lodges are very Tribe-specific, same with Lodge of Wrath and a few others.<br /> But I admit, it could be a good idea to lower the Tribe-requirement into being an exception rather than a rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:27:34-07:00","id":270979,"title":"","content":"Thing with the lodge of the lake is that it started out as a lodge and is now a massive bale hound cult to lamashtu. But hey, were all amazing uratha, why shouldn't we enjoy power?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T12:19:39-07:00","id":271024,"title":"","content":"I like the way the Lodges kind of feel like you are gaining access to a nice close network... It feels very close-knit IMO and I think that they did 'prestige classes' fluff-wise as great as krewes can be fun to build up (Here's another vote for guidelines to creating your own Lodges!).<br /> As said earlier in the thread, I dislike that there are quite stringent prerequisites and you don't get much bang for your buck once you're in the Lodge... The ability you get should be better and make you want to place your Uratha in there through crunch benefits they can gain along with the whole fluff factor of this prestigious Lodge that the character has an Aspiration into joining one day (I think wanting to join a Lodge would make a great long-term aspiration for a starting character). I also think each Lodge needs a boost to a Renown to show you are a respected Uratha that made it into the clubhouse, so to speak.<br /> The fluff and descriptions have always been pretty cool though, reading some does make me want to join in what these guys are about and what they do, they just sound awesome. Its a pity many are hard to work towards and then you don't get much of a reward when you're there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T17:20:52-07:00","id":271229,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I was never taken by Lodges. Between pack and tribe, I felt there was plenty of organizations and never really felt that another layer was needed. I never really liked Legacies for Mage, either. I did, however, dig on Bloodlines. Thinking about it, what I liked about them is that they <b>aren't</b> another layer, they are a refinement of clan. I'd like Lodges more if they were along those lines (and they kind are, halfway). I'd like to see them as regional/ideological sects or refinements within a tribe. These Bone Shadows have a particular way of dealing with ghosts that differs from most of the tribe or these Iron Masters focus on business and acquiring wealth in order to influence humanity. That sort of thing. I'm less enamored with the prestige class approach, where it is just another template that gives you more powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T19:49:23-07:00","id":271321,"title":"","content":"I think the benefits of Lodges could easily be solved by members gaining a Favored Renown, and Influence Dots related to their Patron and what the Lodge is focusing on. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T04:07:30-07:00","id":271522,"title":"","content":"I hope that Lodges are different this time around.<br /> <br /> A player of mine loved lodges for the fact that they brought some specific bonds and connections into the game. I think he was right, but many of the lodges presented were just plain crazy.<br /> Others were so dull you found little to no reason why a pack of diverse PC's should care to connect with a bunch of Uratha who had gotten it wrong.<br /> <br /> I always felt the options given were narrow-minded and far too dense to build a chronicle around.<br /> Lodges were a bit like &quot;the very special club for very special wolves&quot; or simply: a frathouse.<br /> And sometimes a very boring one.<br /> <br /> They were groups that had a common connection but that ultimately fail to create interest in their views or their causes for PC's.<br /> Mainly because Lodges were so specific or nit-picky on who they allowed that many players felt they came of as elitist and game-stopping.<br /> It was like the worlds tiniest political party without any pull for votes because they lack a popular agenda.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone join that? To be with the cool kids? Lodges were a serious flaw in my opinion. Sometimes an interesting flaw, but most of the times it felt like an attempt to make another layer of fraternization that was not needed.<br /> <br /> The best lodges were few and far between, but those that went more towards mystical societies with interesting views on origins and the hisil I found to be more interesting. The mystery society with a focus on hisil or the cult that is slowly going nuts from the inside are good lodges that would be fun to use in a game. Lodges with norse myths, greek myths or similar we-have seen-this-done-500-times-already are not so interesting.<br /> <br /> But then the requirements were just ludicrus, and any group of PC's would go: &quot;Oh, I'm not a Storm-Lord&quot; followed by a sad face. The ones who did play Storm-Lords did not even care about the lodges. Why would they? They were awesome without them!<br /> <br /> Also something I would like to see: Lodges more akin to Covenants. 4 or 5 of those.Large-scale loose fit structures with a clear interest in you and your packs beliefs. Maybe with different views on creation myths (Father moon and Mother wolf anyone?), on the World of Darkness in general and on how to tackle the different challenges of a larger scale. Would be fun for something bigger than pack-scale games.It is always more fun with inclusive groups who want your players than a group that actually goes out f its way to make it hard for the ST to introduce them. Seriously. That sucks.<br /> <br /> Also: A how to make your own lodge chart would be totally cool. :-)<br /> (Just don't make it into something similar to that dry and boring spirit-flowchart in GMC)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T20:41:59-07:00","id":271975,"title":"","content":"As many have expressed already, a little consistency would be nice with Lodges in the future as they've tended to be a bit all over the place in terms of theme, prerequisites, and benefits. I'm not advocating for a complete departure from that paradigm, but bringing them a little closer together would go a long way to resolve some of the issues they present. I'd also like to see a little more from the Pillar Lodges, I really dig the idea that they form major branches of the tribes themselves and therefore they should be a bit more prominent as a result. <br /> <br /> Smaller, more niche, or prestige lodges I'm somewhat on the fence about. They have their place, but since you're only allowed to be in a single Lodge at a time it feels weird. Why would my character who has been a member of the Lodge of Thunder for decades renounce his alliance with them so he can join the Lodge of Scars? I can come up with a few in-context reasons, but the short answer is that they probably wouldn't. It almost feels to me like there should be a second category of Lodges or something like Lodges to fulfill this, but I can understand the need to keep things relatively simple. I'm not sure there's a simple answer to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T21:03:13-07:00","id":271982,"title":"","content":"Yeah, core pillars lodges sounds a pretty cool standing stone, design wise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T09:02:10-07:00","id":272251,"title":"","content":"I think if there has to be large prerequisites, make the boon you get for joining all the better. These should likely be secondary Lodges for more endgame stuff, so the pillar lodges can be joined more easily and be a large part of the game until there is reason and experience enough to join one of the more legendary Lodges, much like there are powerful Entitlements that need high 5+ Wyrd in Changeling, but give benefits to help with the cons for having Wyrd up that high, Werewolf could stand to have options like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T10:15:54-07:00","id":272325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=271522#post271522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also something I would like to see: Lodges more akin to Covenants. 4 or 5 of those.Large-scale loose fit structures with a clear interest in you and your packs beliefs. Maybe with different views on creation myths (<b>Father moon and Mother wolf anyone?</b>), on the World of Darkness in general and on how to tackle the different challenges of a larger scale. Would be fun for something bigger than pack-scale games.It is always more fun with inclusive groups who want your players than a group that actually goes out f its way to make it hard for the ST to introduce them. Seriously. That sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a note on the bolded part - as has been revealed in an earlier blog post as I recall, the flip-flopping of that terminology is in the new core.<br /> <br /> Not saying that such a lodge couldn't take that further, of course. I'm simply pointing that out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T10:32:55-07:00","id":272334,"title":"","content":"Changeling had entitlements, which had more of a supernatural effect on your character, giving them a title and all (but not a Title).<br /> <br /> You essentially became part of something big, becoming something big yourself.<br /> <br /> There were also eldritch entitlements, I think, which had a high Wyrd (power stat) requirement, but offered more power and more of a change, in return.<br /> <br /> Obviously entitlements work differently than lodges, but keeping in mind it is led by another totem there could be some spiritual influence that has more of an affect on the werewolf. Sort of turning it a bit more magath, I suppose. Instead of being part spirit-of-the-hunt, you'd be part spirit-of-the-hunt and part spirit-of-storms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T17:51:24-07:00","id":272599,"title":"","content":"Hmm, personally I like most of the lodges. But I think some of them could have been taken back a bit, considering they didn't really emphasise the 'werewolf' part in them. And a lot of the lodges in Splintered required you to set the games at those locales, this limiting the game a lot unless your goal was to involve uratha in those countries/places. I like most of the lodges in Tribes of the Moon, the Blood Talon ones are especially cool. A huge part of what I think a lodge should be is emphasis something about the Auspice/Tribe or just Uratha in general. If a lodge is more about trying to deal with spiritual concept (Fallen Idol) or just extremely narrow focus (jewish cahaliths?) it takes away from the feeling of werewolf. And considering Forsaken can easily become Shaman the Summoning if not handled well, this is important.<br /> <br /> One lodge I think could use some retooling would be;<br /> <br /> -Lodge of the Saviour is a Lodge I like and it gives a nice background to the uratha character. But I think it would help this lodge a lot to tie it to an actual Christian werewolf myth: <a href=\"http://werewolves.monstrous.com/benandanti_werewolves.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://werewolves.monstrous.com/bena...werewolves.htm</a><br /> That, and maybe not involve Maeljin unless needed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:05:52-07:00","id":272962,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Lodges done in the way for there to be 'eldritch' style ones... Really my only real issues with Werewolf have been that there is so much crunch to remember that you need the core by your side to check things consistently and that the flavour of totem spirits in the rockies wasn't really my bag... Though changing the scenery is incredibly easy to do and I do like spirits, so really for me it comes to crunch. I'd like to see a more streamlined set of rules to keep it in line with the other splats that have quite easy to remember rulings and most char stuff is on the character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:06:04-07:00","id":273405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=271975#post271975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smaller, more niche, or prestige lodges I'm somewhat on the fence about. They have their place, but since you're only allowed to be in a single Lodge at a time it feels weird. Why would my character who has been a member of the Lodge of Thunder for decades renounce his alliance with them so he can join the Lodge of Scars? I can come up with a few in-context reasons, but the short answer is that they probably wouldn't. It almost feels to me like there should be a second category of Lodges or something like Lodges to fulfill this, but I can understand the need to keep things relatively simple. I'm not sure there's a simple answer to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the exclusive and even regional feel of some lodges, but I also agree that there should be some further distinction for lodges that seem to ask quite a lot from their members and give a lot in return-- the &quot;first in&quot; mentality and penalties to Harmony of the Lodge of Night and the redonkulous bonuses they get, versus say the Lodge of Metal, which is just a collection of hobbyists who get a nice bonus to their crafting rolls. They feel completely different, but they're both called Lodges.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2279-mister-wizard","name":"Mister Wizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:25:38-07:00","id":273426,"title":"","content":"Mots are cool. I'd like to see more lodges like them. It doesn't specifically have to be more mots, but I dig the cultural lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T03:38:25-07:00","id":273567,"title":"","content":"Some useful feedback here, chaps. As Bunyip mentioned, this is a side discussion - our corebook drafts are done.<br /> <br /> We have some ideas about where to go with Lodges, but it's good to get additional points of view about what works and what doesn't with the current style of Lodges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T04:31:34-07:00","id":273605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=270365#post270365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also be nice if Lodges were something one could come and go from. Perhaps be a member of them for a few years, but then when one has changed as a person, it'd be ok to leave, perhaps to found a lodge of your own, or join another that fits who you've become more. It would also make it contrast nicely with Legacies and Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this concept. Lodges that don't demand a life-long commitment, especially if an Uratha departs to join a more prestigious or powerful lodge. Extrapolating from this, I'd also like some of the higher power, more exclusive lodges to have their prerequisites include membership in one of the lesser lodges - if you can't succeed at being a member in one of those, you'll never make the grade for the more exclusive lodges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T04:49:18-07:00","id":273607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=273605#post273605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this concept. Lodges that don't demand a life-long commitment, especially if an Uratha departs to join a more prestigious or powerful lodge. Extrapolating from this, I'd also like some of the higher power, more exclusive lodges to have their prerequisites include membership in one of the lesser lodges - if you can't succeed at being a member in one of those, you'll never make the grade for the more exclusive lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that is interesting. It plays well with the bottom-up social structure, too... Sort of like your new in the neighborhood, someone invites you to their barbeque, and half the people there are on the.same bowling team or civic society or whatever... Not *everyone* in the area gets to be part of that club, but at least you get to flip burgers with some of the best of them...<br /> <br /> Maybe my analogy is too domestic, but having multiple sets of social/pack/lodge/territory ties/responsibilities now sounds like a situation that wouldn't crop up in particularly volatile areas. 'Peacetime' packs would certainly have more to do, though..!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T07:55:32-07:00","id":273825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=273605#post273605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this concept. Lodges that don't demand a life-long commitment, especially if an Uratha departs to join a more prestigious or powerful lodge. Extrapolating from this, I'd also like some of the higher power, more exclusive lodges to have their prerequisites include membership in one of the lesser lodges - if you can't succeed at being a member in one of those, you'll never make the grade for the more exclusive lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, something akin to the difference between entitlements and eldritch orders?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T09:06:21-07:00","id":273909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=273605#post273605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this concept. Lodges that don't demand a life-long commitment, especially if an Uratha departs to join a more prestigious or powerful lodge. Extrapolating from this, I'd also like some of the higher power, more exclusive lodges to have their prerequisites include membership in one of the lesser lodges - if you can't succeed at being a member in one of those, you'll never make the grade for the more exclusive lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whee! I did something a dev likes!<br /> <br /> When I was writing that up, I remembered that I thought that it was a bummer for people having to go until they were old badasses who had never joined a Lodge to join the Lodge of Scars. <br /> I suppose there was implicit leaving and joining going on, wasn't there a mention that one would generally use Rite of Contrition towards totems of lodges and tribes one left? Or am I just dreaming that up? It quite often is.<br /> That's not something I liked anyhow, I hope it was just my stupid mind making it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:23:27-07:00","id":274006,"title":"","content":"It kind of reminds me of the Seven Soldiers comic from Grant Morrison. A sort of grand sacred hunt, people are chosen for it (perhaps by a totem) or volunteer or volunteered by others.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it makes me think of a lodge, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T16:46:16-07:00","id":275051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=273605#post273605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this concept. Lodges that don't demand a life-long commitment, especially if an Uratha departs to join a more prestigious or powerful lodge. Extrapolating from this, I'd also like some of the higher power, more exclusive lodges to have their prerequisites include membership in one of the lesser lodges - if you can't succeed at being a member in one of those, you'll never make the grade for the more exclusive lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have a particularly powerful spirit be the patron of both (Crow for example), or have a powerful patron for one lodge (Crow) and then a lesser choir member (Thief of Shinies) be the patron of the weaker lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T19:52:47-07:00","id":275151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=275051#post275051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Have a particularly powerful spirit be the patron of both (Crow for example), or have a powerful patron for one lodge (Crow) and then a lesser choir member (Thief of Shinies) be the patron of the weaker lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You heard it here folks! Thief of Shinies is now canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:48:00-07:00","id":276403,"title":"","content":"Will there be any mention of clutches in the book? (For those who don't know/remember what I'm talking about, the clutch is an organization or gathering of multiple packs. Basically how werewolves get to a Tier 2/regional setting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T09:12:14-07:00","id":276415,"title":"","content":"I can't say much on that, I'm afraid, although I will point you to this particular line in Stew's Hunting Grounds blog post - &quot;Want to run a story involving tense relations between a powerful union of Uratha, a demented spirit-goddess, and an idigam? Set the story in Bristol.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll also say that no-one on the dev team particularly likes the term 'clutch', as it's not very evocative.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T13:59:41-07:00","id":276622,"title":"","content":"I always liked <i><b>Cairn</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:52:17-07:00","id":276811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=276622#post276622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked <i><b>Cairn</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You got your Apocalypse chocolate in our Forsaken peanut butter! :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:57:19-07:00","id":276813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=276415#post276415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also say that no-one on the dev team particularly likes the term 'clutch', as it's not very evocative.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first reaction was, &quot;I thought a clutch was the collective noun for spiders.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I looked it up. It's not. It's the collective noun for chickens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T17:51:40-07:00","id":276866,"title":"","content":"Yes. Clutch doesn't really seem to fit the Uratha, even if you avoid the fowl association, and caern does with Apocalypse (from what little I know of Apocalypse) but less so with Forsaken. Locus is actually pretty apt.<br /> <br /> Of course I can't really offer any useful alternatives. Claw, fang, are too pat. Werewolf looks like it has a bit of a Slasher bent to it, and I read a book recently called a Blood of Killers, suggesting that the collective noun for murderers should be a Blood. But that seems to infringe on Vampire. I've always liked the First Tongue, I can imagine something coming from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-09-2014, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T18:52:04-07:00","id":276893,"title":"","content":"Which books were clutches mentioned in in 1e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T18:58:24-07:00","id":276897,"title":"","content":"The Rage, the Player's Guide. I'm unsure if it's been mentioned elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-09-2014, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T20:28:53-07:00","id":276952,"title":"","content":"I really liked the idea behind the Clutch section in The Rage, but Clutch is a bit of a silly term for it.<br /> I'd prefer something with a slight military undertone as well as a technical meaning as simply a group, like Cohort.<br /> Edit: or Coalition. Those would be my submissions for rebranding attempts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","user":"Red 9","date":". 10-09-2014, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T23:15:34-07:00","id":277016,"title":"","content":"&quot;Compact&quot; would have been perfect. Unfortunately, Hunter got it first.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rout/Route&quot; is an alternative collective noun for wolves, with an unfortunate modern meaning, but archaically, it <i>did</i> mean a detachment of soldiers.<br /> <br /> There's also the more bland &quot;Band&quot;, which has a faint military connotation, but probably doesn't quite work when people would associate it with rock bands rather than marching bands. There's also &quot;Company&quot;, which runs into some pretty obvious problems.<br /> <br /> Bleh. The problem with words with military feels (which I agree would be good) is that Werewolves don't feel as disciplined as a military, so you very quickly start wandering into words for <i>incompetent</i> soldiers, and there's a reason groups of those tend to fall apart.<br /> <br /> Hrm. You know what I'd do? I wouldn't pick an English word at all. Make something up in First Tongue and say it has no translation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T23:49:00-07:00","id":277029,"title":"","content":"'Company of wolves' has a wonderfully poetic ring to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T06:22:57-07:00","id":277159,"title":"","content":"A Howling of Uratha, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T06:49:09-07:00","id":277180,"title":"","content":"I'm partial to a &quot;Murder&quot; myself. But then, I pick &quot;Murder&quot; for most congregations of violent creatures, so that's kind of redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T09:03:08-07:00","id":277280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=276811#post276811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You got your Apocalypse chocolate in our Forsaken peanut butter! :-P</div> </div> </div> </div>Two flavors that go well together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T11:20:05-07:00","id":277398,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;band&quot; is also the term used for the villages/communities that made up a Native American nation, particularly those of Algonquin stock. So &quot;band&quot; could work that way, but like Errol said, it conjures images of musical groups. &quot;Nation&quot; is another possibility, but the word has awfully large connotations; it's probably more suitable for Tier 3 games. If we could translate some word that could mean a domicile and a meeting place into the First Tongue, that might be best. Otherwise, &quot;Cairn&quot; is looking better the more I look for alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:04:45-07:00","id":277463,"title":"","content":"A Howling or Howl of Uratha sounds nice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:11:39-07:00","id":277472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=276811#post276811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You got your Apocalypse chocolate in our Forsaken peanut butter! :-P</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T13:25:49-07:00","id":277521,"title":"","content":"A Howling actually does sound pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T18:33:41-07:00","id":277735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=276893#post276893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which books were clutches mentioned in in 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rage. This is the sidebar on the term.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Clutch, Noun.</b><br /> Why the term \u201cclutch?\u201d Two reasons.The first definition of the word is this: \u201ca hand, claw, talon or paw in the act of grasping.\u201d Werewolves know that attempting such an alliance is a far grasp. But nothing worth doing is without risk and effort, right? The second definition \u2014 and by far the more vulgar of the two \u2014 is as follows: \u201cthe complete set of eggs produced and/or incubated at the same time; also, a brood of chickens.\u201d The term is dismissive, one used by Forsaken outside the alliance. Such a term derogatorily suggests that those who would rely on wolves beyond the pack for aid and leadership are, of course, chickens. Unfit for the instinct of wolves, given over to the pecking order of cowardly birds. It\u2019s an ugly implication, and one that a cynic would be wise not to voice too loudly around a group of allied werewolves already on the defensive. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T12:14:50-07:00","id":278973,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, while I know folks are busy developing and writing for other books that aren't done...can we get more delicious spoilers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T14:25:37-07:00","id":279073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=278973#post278973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, while I know folks are busy developing and writing for other books that aren't done...can we get more delicious spoilers?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been quite a while, true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T15:35:18-07:00","id":279129,"title":"","content":"Well I hinted at something with my last post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, what do you want to know about? Can't guarantee I can offer up anything to appease the hungry masses, but you never know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T16:17:18-07:00","id":279148,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested to know if anything has changed about Wounds and Wound-tainted spirits. I know it was mentioned that it is not necessary for a spirit to be of a negative concept to be Wound-tainted, that a tainted spirit of Joy is just as possible as a tainted spirit of Murder. Interested to hear any details that you could relate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T17:06:25-07:00","id":279168,"title":"","content":"I think it was said a while ago that the tracking/hunting rules were improved upon, unless I'm misremembering this. I am curious as to how this has been done. Also, Stew's blog touched upon Uratha being able to breed with fellow Uratha in the new iteration of the game; with that particular Harmony sins out of the way, what other Breaking Points might have been in the old Harmony system that wouldn't be present in this one? Unless... that's violating non-disclosure, in which case that's alright. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T17:49:27-07:00","id":279195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279148#post279148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested to know if anything has changed about Wounds and Wound-tainted spirits. I know it was mentioned that it is not necessary for a spirit to be of a negative concept to be Wound-tainted, that a tainted spirit of Joy is just as possible as a tainted spirit of Murder. Interested to hear any details that you could relate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best question would be: Are there spirits of murder that aren't considered wounded? IE: With a natural environment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T18:14:29-07:00","id":279249,"title":"","content":"I was told this in another thread, the one about rites, pardon for not quoting but it's from Acrozatarim. It was about one of the rites banishing wound spirits.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, Wounded spirits aren't 'bad' spirits. They're <i>corrupted</i>. Hatred, anger, death, murder, pain, anguish spirits are all perfectly normal spirits. The creatures that infest the pustules of taint that are Wounds have been infected and changed. A Wounded spirit of happiness would be hurled through a Wound by the Banish rite; an unWounded spirit of hatred would not.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T18:23:17-07:00","id":279257,"title":"","content":"So what he's saying is that they aren't bad spirits, they just made bad decisions?[/badjoke]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T19:02:13-07:00","id":279297,"title":"","content":"Here's a lead-up, and a question, to the writers.<br /> <br /> Could you see yourselves doing books similar to the clan books and upcoming covenant book for Vampire the Requiem, but for Werewolf tribes and auspices?<br /> <br /> That is to say, a book detailing the many aspects of an auspice or tribe (or all the auspices or tribes in a single book) from in-world stories, with added mechanics and rules in the back? I ask because while we know each auspice gets a gift, and there's a few tribal merits in the merit teaser, we haven't seen that much of a mechanical difference, for the tribes, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T00:04:22-07:00","id":279425,"title":"","content":"To answer your last comment first, you'll see more tribal differences with the Siskur-dah Rite.<br /> <br /> As for your first question, I could definitely see such books (and would happily help write them) but I am neither Stew nor OPP. <br /> <br /> I would imagine such decisions will be driven by the market. Basically, if werewolf fans vote with their cash, more werewolf books will be written! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T00:17:31-07:00","id":279428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279249#post279249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;So, Wounded spirits aren't 'bad' spirits. They're <i>corrupted</i>. Hatred, anger, death, murder, pain, anguish spirits are all perfectly normal spirits. The creatures that infest the pustules of taint that are Wounds have been infected and changed. A Wounded spirit of happiness would be hurled through a Wound by the Banish rite; an unWounded spirit of hatred would not.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I only see here potential for <b>Mage</b> crossover? Don't this &quot;corruption&quot; stink it as Abyss influence on spirits?<br /> <br /> And what does this mean in the context that Malejin could be Demon Princess of <b>Inferno</b> realm ( Lower Deaths about Vices )?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T02:49:35-07:00","id":279472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279297#post279297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a lead-up, and a question, to the writers.<br /> <br /> Could you see yourselves doing books similar to the clan books and upcoming covenant book for Vampire the Requiem, but for Werewolf tribes and auspices?<br /> <br /> That is to say, a book detailing the many aspects of an auspice or tribe (or all the auspices or tribes in a single book) from in-world stories, with added mechanics and rules in the back? I ask because while we know each auspice gets a gift, and there's a few tribal merits in the merit teaser, we haven't seen that much of a mechanical difference, for the tribes, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think that would be awesome, but we'll have to wait and see what folks above my pay grade decide on that front. Although, honestly, if folks want to see more books for <b>Forsaken</b>, buy the hell out of the core book. I can't promise anything obviously, but that'll very likely increase the chances of more books for the line. All I know is that I have told Stew that I'd like to volunteer for all of the things, when and if they become available. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T04:51:42-07:00","id":279510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279428#post279428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I only see here potential for <b>Mage</b> crossover? Don't this &quot;corruption&quot; stink it as Abyss influence on spirits?<br /> <br /> And what does this mean in the context that Malejin could be Demon Princess of <b>Inferno</b> realm ( Lower Deaths about Vices )?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The corruption is from Wounds, which aren't related to the Abyss. <i>Inferno</i> already links the Maeljin Incarna as Dukes of Hell.<br /> <br /> And thank you for your answers, Bunyip and strider1276.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-13-2014, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T04:59:20-07:00","id":279515,"title":"","content":"But if Maeljin Incarna are Dukes of Hell, that means the Wound are corrupting both Joy and Murder spirits with &quot;sins&quot;, don't it? So all Wound spirits are about &quot;evil&quot;, not &quot;otherness&quot;? Like even negative spirits are bout &quot;evil&quot; - Murder spirit becomes spirits of &quot;evil Murders&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T06:01:33-07:00","id":279572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279148#post279148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested to know if anything has changed about Wounds and Wound-tainted spirits. I know it was mentioned that it is not necessary for a spirit to be of a negative concept to be Wound-tainted, that a tainted spirit of Joy is just as possible as a tainted spirit of Murder. Interested to hear any details that you could relate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't think of anything else to relate about Wounds and Wounded spirits at the moment. There's obviously going to be limited wordcount on the topic in the final book as we've got so much to cram into the book!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279168#post279168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was said a while ago that the tracking/hunting rules were improved upon, unless I'm misremembering this. I am curious as to how this has been done. Also, Stew's blog touched upon Uratha being able to breed with fellow Uratha in the new iteration of the game; with that particular Harmony sins out of the way, what other Breaking Points might have been in the old Harmony system that wouldn't be present in this one? Unless... that's violating non-disclosure, in which case that's alright. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The new tracking rules are Bunyip's masterpiece, but they were quite a late addition so we really need to wait and see how they look once they're out of playtesting.<br /> <br /> Having used them in my own playtest game, I'm pleased with how they work. It lets werewolves be amazing trackers, while also offering the chance for meaningful challenge and contest.<br /> <br /> Hmm, old Harmony sins? Not sure, off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279195#post279195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best question would be: Are there spirits of murder that aren't considered wounded? IE: With a natural environment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279249#post279249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was told this in another thread, the one about rites, pardon for not quoting but it's from Acrozatarim. It was about one of the rites banishing wound spirits.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, Wounded spirits aren't 'bad' spirits. They're <i>corrupted</i>. Hatred, anger, death, murder, pain, anguish spirits are all perfectly normal spirits. The creatures that infest the pustules of taint that are Wounds have been infected and changed. A Wounded spirit of happiness would be hurled through a Wound by the Banish rite; an unWounded spirit of hatred would not.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279297#post279297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a lead-up, and a question, to the writers.<br /> <br /> Could you see yourselves doing books similar to the clan books and upcoming covenant book for Vampire the Requiem, but for Werewolf tribes and auspices?<br /> <br /> That is to say, a book detailing the many aspects of an auspice or tribe (or all the auspices or tribes in a single book) from in-world stories, with added mechanics and rules in the back? I ask because while we know each auspice gets a gift, and there's a few tribal merits in the merit teaser, we haven't seen that much of a mechanical difference, for the tribes, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, would be nice, but that decision is above my pay grade <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In terms of mechanical difference, there's a fair few bits and pieces - the Affinity Gifts, merits, rites and Siskur-Dah benefits, as well as various modifiers to things like Gift use against favoured prey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279428#post279428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I only see here potential for <b>Mage</b> crossover? Don't this &quot;corruption&quot; stink it as Abyss influence on spirits?<br /> <br /> And what does this mean in the context that Malejin could be Demon Princess of <b>Inferno</b> realm ( Lower Deaths about Vices )?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, the corruption of Wounds is not the same thing as Abyssal influence, but you could certainly run it that way if you wanted.<br /> <br /> There is some material about the Maeljin and the Lower Depths already somewhere, I think, but I can't remember exactly where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T07:41:44-07:00","id":279617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279572#post279572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is some material about the Maeljin and the Lower Depths already somewhere, I think, but I can't remember exactly where.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, in the Idigam Chronicle? Or somewhere in the nWoD vastness? 'Cuz the latter would mean <b>Inferno</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:00:48-07:00","id":279625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279617#post279617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in, in the Idigam Chronicle? Or somewhere in the nWoD vastness? 'Cuz the latter would mean <b>Inferno</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I meant in nWoD in general, so in Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:06:38-07:00","id":279626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279148#post279148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested to know if anything has changed about Wounds and Wound-tainted spirits. I know it was mentioned that it is not necessary for a spirit to be of a negative concept to be Wound-tainted, that a tainted spirit of Joy is just as possible as a tainted spirit of Murder. Interested to hear any details that you could relate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wounds are written post-<b>Inferno</b>, so while the text about them in Idigam never includes the words &quot;Lower Depths,&quot; it does describe how Wounds split open to reveal gateways to somewhere <i>other</i> than the Shadow, that the maeljin aren't spirits, and that spirits feeding in Wounds get corrupted by the energies of wherever-it-is the Wound links to.<br /> <br /> The only line Stew cut was one raising the possibility of Wounded Uratha, as Bale Hounds are too big a kettle of fish to raise in one line if we're not then going to devote any time to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:13:16-07:00","id":279633,"title":"","content":"Maeljin aren't spirits now? That's kind of disappointing.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Wounded Uratha. But possibly rebranded with a different name, since that makes it sound like they're hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-13-2014, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:28:06-07:00","id":279657,"title":"","content":"Everythig's toolbox. They can be spirits if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:42:57-07:00","id":279686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279633#post279633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maeljin aren't spirits now? That's kind of disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, Inferno demons aren't &quot;spirits&quot;, either, but that's mostly because they've taken on new characteristics that takes them outside the usual dynamic of the Shadow Realm.<br /> <br /> The Maeljin are supposed to be FUBAR, anyway, why call them &quot;spirits&quot; anymore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:15:51-07:00","id":279825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279626#post279626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wounds are written post-<b>Inferno</b>, so while the text about them in Idigam never includes the words &quot;Lower Depths,&quot; it does describe how Wounds split open to reveal gateways to somewhere <i>other</i> than the Shadow, that the maeljin aren't spirits, and that spirits feeding in Wounds get corrupted by the energies of wherever-it-is the Wound links to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the Wounds spirits are <b>Inferno</b> demons, it still means they are &quot;corrupt spirits&quot;. Or rather &quot;sin-fixated spirits&quot; - <b>Inferno</b> demons can be any of ephermeral entity, they just &quot;wrapped&quot; by Hells energies and are dedicated to making more &quot;evil&quot; ( a Vice variant, really ). You can have changed by Inferno spirits, ghost or even astral beings - and all of them are demons according to book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:25:16-07:00","id":279835,"title":"","content":"I really hope Maeljin (and Bale Hounds, because Bale Hounds) are high on the priority list for supplements. They aren't super easy to convert now that Vice no longer works the way that it used to and the idea that the seven deadly sins have metaphysical weight is no longer part of the setting.<br /> <br /> We could probably use an Inferno second edition, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T11:50:31-07:00","id":279967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279835#post279835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope Maeljin (and Bale Hounds, because Bale Hounds) are high on the priority list for supplements. They aren't super easy to convert now that Vice no longer works the way that it used to and the idea that the seven deadly sins have metaphysical weight is no longer part of the setting.<br /> <br /> We could probably use an Inferno second edition, even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure first then Bale Hounds!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:05:06-07:00","id":280656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279835#post279835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope Maeljin (and Bale Hounds, because Bale Hounds) are high on the priority list for supplements. They aren't super easy to convert now that Vice no longer works the way that it used to and the idea that the seven deadly sins have metaphysical weight is no longer part of the setting.<br /> <br /> We could probably use an Inferno second edition, even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with everything, except Seven Deadly Sins don't having metaphysical weight. In <b>Mage</b> you still got 7*7 Masques. In <b>Werewolf</b> there are still Maeljin's, seven on them based on Deadly Sins. in my games I let players choose any Virtue and Vice they like, just connect it with older system, for backward compatybility - like player choose Vice Arogance and wirte just after it &quot;( Pride )&quot;. It saves a lot of trouble.<br /> <br /> But I agree - I'm also counting that Bale Hounds book ( and maybe new Inferno ) are high on priority...<br /> <br /> Pure will be in 2ed corebook, so they don't need new treatment any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:18:56-07:00","id":280662,"title":"","content":"Bare bones Pure will be in corebook, and they'll need detail more urgently than Bale Hounds, IMO.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds may be cool, but they're far and away a less present antagonist threat for everyday Forsaken than the Pure are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T02:10:06-07:00","id":280751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=280662#post280662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bare bones Pure will be in corebook, and they'll need detail more urgently than Bale Hounds, IMO.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds may be cool, but they're far and away a less present antagonist threat for everyday Forsaken than the Pure are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am glad to see that Pure is getting some love in 2nd ed. Yay!<br /> The quality of work given to Pure tribes in 1 ed was beyond anything I had hoped for. Really good stuff.<br /> <br /> I hope future supplements touch more on both Pure and Bale hounds. give a more in-depth look on both.<br /> <br /> Some things I would love to see (future supplements):<br /> - one or two more Pure tribes added to the lot.<br /> - If possible get the excellent Abrar Ajmal back to make the art for 2nd ed.<br /> - Bale Hounds in their own packs or lodges?<br /> - Expanded material on Pure's Wolfblooded and how they operate.<br /> - Information on Anshega or Uratha who turn on their own and join the ranks of the enemy. Renegades!<br /> <br /> I would love this.<br /> <br /> Back to 2 ed.<br /> Will Talens and fetishes work as they did in 1 ed?<br /> Will Zi'ir get more info? They always felt a bit lacking.<br /> Will there be original dices made for the edition? Not very important. But hey! Nice if we got some new ones! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:49:21-07:00","id":280811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279825#post279825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if the Wounds spirits are <b>Inferno</b> demons, it still means they are &quot;corrupt spirits&quot;. Or rather &quot;sin-fixated spirits&quot; - <b>Inferno</b> demons can be any of ephermeral entity, they just &quot;wrapped&quot; by Hells energies and are dedicated to making more &quot;evil&quot; ( a Vice variant, really ). You can have changed by Inferno spirits, ghost or even astral beings - and all of them are demons according to book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty good guess what he is referring to is while there are some elements that seem common to the entities of the Lower Depths a lot of it as a term is really just a collective, &quot;Lol Nope areas we only have some vague ideas about.&quot; With the intermingling of those disparate....things....and areas of the Tellurian( to borrow the CWoD terminology) that are more familiar to various bits of the NWoD creating an appropriately scary sense of uncertainty over what is what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T04:12:54-07:00","id":280818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279168#post279168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was said a while ago that the tracking/hunting rules were improved upon, unless I'm misremembering this. I am curious as to how this has been done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked Stew about releasing the new tracking rules here as a playtest opportunity for the forums. Stew had planned to do it himself as a Forsaken Friday update, but since that time I guess he's been swamped with his double development duties. Hopefully he'll get a chance some time soon. *fingers crossed*.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T04:15:37-07:00","id":280821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279572#post279572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new tracking rules are Bunyip's masterpiece, but they were quite a late addition so we really need to wait and see how they look once they're out of playtesting.<br /> <br /> Having used them in my own playtest game, I'm pleased with how they work. It lets werewolves be amazing trackers, while also offering the chance for meaningful challenge and contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good feedback, having an idea of the system masters in your game. Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:11:36-07:00","id":281017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=280656#post280656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree with everything, except Seven Deadly Sins don't having metaphysical weight. In <b>Mage</b> you still got 7*7 Masques. In <b>Werewolf</b> there are still Maeljin's, seven on them based on Deadly Sins. in my games I let players choose any Virtue and Vice they like, just connect it with older system, for backward compatybility - like player choose Vice Arogance and wirte just after it &quot;( Pride )&quot;. It saves a lot of trouble.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's far from clear that either of those things are still true in 2e, and it's fairly likely that Masques at the very least aren't. And not all Vices map nicely to one of the sins.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind Inferno and the Maeljin moving away from being strictly sin based, toward something else, either. If they represent inversions of concepts, or parasitic or corruptive forces in a more general sense, it'd open up some more interesting options. There's a lot of ways they could go if they're not bound by the limitations of needing to fall along Vice spirit lines. Vice can just become a vector by which they go about being parasitic, chosen solely because it's an easy way to manipulate people. The ends would be more centered around needing to break or consume things in particular ways.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:16:04-07:00","id":281021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=280662#post280662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bare bones Pure will be in corebook, and they'll need detail more urgently than Bale Hounds, IMO.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds may be cool, but they're far and away a less present antagonist threat for everyday Forsaken than the Pure are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and I don't mind that at all; high on the list doesn't need to be at the top, just, hopefully, not 3+ years out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:19:52-07:00","id":281025,"title":"","content":"I don't like the tendency to shunt the source of the evils of the World of Darkness into alien realms. Terms like Lower Depths shouldn't pop up in Werewolf lore, beyond &quot;Someone was in the Wound last night, they kept babbling about Lower Depths until I tore their throat out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Traditionally, the first Wound was formed where Father Wolf was slain by the Uratha. And while the Maeljin may not have spawned from it, at least one of them supposedly still 'lives' there.<br /> <br /> While the game's gotten rid of the seven sins concept, as it's a version of our world (but darker), the seven sins would still exist. I could see the Maeljin sticking to those 9 werewolf sins, twisting spirits to those causes, or broadening their scope and possibly having other, new Maeljin Incarna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2014, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:22:54-07:00","id":281030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=280751#post280751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am glad to see that Pure is getting some love in 2nd ed. Yay!<br /> The quality of work given to Pure tribes in 1 ed was beyond anything I had hoped for. Really good stuff.<br /> <br /> I hope future supplements touch more on both Pure and Bale hounds. give a more in-depth look on both.<br /> <br /> Some things I would love to see (future supplements):<br /> - one or two more Pure tribes added to the lot.<br /> - If possible get the excellent Abrar Ajmal back to make the art for 2nd ed.<br /> - Bale Hounds in their own packs or lodges?<br /> - Expanded material on Pure's Wolfblooded and how they operate.<br /> - Information on Anshega or Uratha who turn on their own and join the ranks of the enemy. Renegades!<br /> <br /> I would love this.<br /> <br /> Back to 2 ed.<br /> Will Talens and fetishes work as they did in 1 ed?<br /> Will Zi'ir get more info? They always felt a bit lacking.<br /> Will there be original dices made for the edition? Not very important. But hey! Nice if we got some new ones! :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like that in 2ed they make Bale Hounds a proper tribe, with Souless Wolf as their totem(since Maeljin aren\u00b4t spirits).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:26:32-07:00","id":281032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281030#post281030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like that in 2ed they make Bale Hounds a proper tribe, with Souless Wolf as their totem(since Maeljin aren\u00b4t spirits).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I liked that option but I liked the others, too, the undercover Lodge and the dark pantheism. I suppose you could have all three, nothing says evil has to work in only one way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:05:57-07:00","id":281104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=279967#post279967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pure first then Bale Hounds!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This would certainly be my priority order, but that may just be because I am desperately eager to write the new mechanics for the 2e Pure. I had a lot of fun hinting at more in-depth things in the corebook's Pure section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=280751#post280751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would love this.<br /> <br /> Back to 2 ed.<br /> Will Talens and fetishes work as they did in 1 ed?<br /> Will Zi'ir get more info? They always felt a bit lacking.<br /> Will there be original dices made for the edition? Not very important. But hey! Nice if we got some new ones! :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetishes work very similarly, but with some new design space added. Talens work differently, although old-style Talens are viable under the new system.<br /> <br /> Zi'ir, not entirely sure, I'd have to read the relevant sections again. Remember that Harmony works rather differently now, though, and being at Harmony 0 under the new system means something quite different to what it did in the old system.<br /> <br /> No idea on dice, that's a Stew Thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=280821#post280821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's good feedback, having an idea of the system masters in your game. Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We used the old tracking rules earlier in the playtest before your stuff had been written, and the comparison between new and old was a positive one. Sadly we haven't had a chance to give it a more extensive run through the wringer as we've moved onto Mage playtesting now, but I do feel confident your new tracking rules are a step up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:59:01-07:00","id":281275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=280751#post280751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If possible get the excellent Abrar Ajmal back to make the art for 2nd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that Abrar Ajmal is to Forsaken what Ron Spencer is to Apocalypse. I cannot second this enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:05:29-07:00","id":281283,"title":"","content":"Yes, I love their work. I'll admit there's a sense of sameness to some of their characters but it's still very evocative of Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:57:56-07:00","id":281336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281025#post281025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the tendency to shunt the source of the evils of the World of Darkness into alien realms. Terms like Lower Depths shouldn't pop up in Werewolf lore, beyond &quot;Someone was in the Wound last night, they kept babbling about Lower Depths until I tore their throat out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Traditionally, the first Wound was formed where Father Wolf was slain by the Uratha. And while the Maeljin may not have spawned from it, at least one of them supposedly still 'lives' there.<br /> <br /> While the game's gotten rid of the seven sins concept, as it's a version of our world (but darker), the seven sins would still exist. I could see the Maeljin sticking to those 9 werewolf sins, twisting spirits to those causes, or broadening their scope and possibly having other, new Maeljin Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inferno=/=The Lower Depths. So you have a lot of stuff to work with that has absolutely nothing to do with 1st editions Vices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:42:07-07:00","id":281493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281017#post281017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind Inferno and the Maeljin moving away from being strictly sin based, toward something else, either. If they represent inversions of concepts, or parasitic or corruptive forces in a more general sense, it'd open up some more interesting options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't this makes them Abyss bound? The Great Void is realm of paradoxes ( and mages Paradoxes )...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:00:14-07:00","id":281641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281336#post281336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inferno=/=The Lower Depths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many writers have stated that Inferno is part of the Lower Depths, for what that's worth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:11:55-07:00","id":281647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281641#post281641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many writers have stated that Inferno is part of the Lower Depths, for what that's worth</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, it's just not ALL of the lower depths. So thankfully a lot of space for wtf is this? We don't know what(insert creepy stuff here) really is. I should have clarified what i meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-14-2014, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:46:11-07:00","id":281727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281032#post281032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked that option but I liked the others, too, the undercover Lodge and the dark pantheism. I suppose you could have all three, nothing says evil has to work in only one way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, slight tangent time. Back when I was in the Camarilla (now Mind's Eye Society), I was the Global Forsaken Storyteller twice. The second time, I started working up a rather comprehensive setting guide/resource for the Bale Hounds. I like to think that I did some interesting things with them. Maybe I'll see if Stew wants me to clean up what I have (I didn't ever get to finish it, for reasons) and take a look at it, for a <b>hypothetical</b> future supplement.<br /> <br /> Because as much as Acrozatarim wants to write Pure? I want to write Bale Hounds. (Although I'd write Pure too, of course. Anything and everything <b>Werewolf</b>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:53:55-07:00","id":281740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281032#post281032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I liked that option but I liked the others, too, the undercover Lodge and the dark pantheism. I suppose you could have all three, nothing says evil has to work in only one way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer them as a Tribe, but each choosing also a patron Maeljin and getting Investments for them, not Gifts, to differentiate them from the other Uratha, with Lodges being options for regular Pure and Forsaken who try to harness their power(and slowly being corrupted) to help in the Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T19:00:45-07:00","id":281799,"title":"","content":"So, how about we get some more merits spoiled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T01:08:44-07:00","id":282043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281727#post281727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because as much as Acrozatarim wants to write Pure? I want to write Bale Hounds. (Although I'd write Pure too, of course. Anything and everything <b>Werewolf</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>As much i very like Acrozatarim ( you really do good work, men! ) you've become my favorite line developer! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So I can assume first supplement after the corebook would about Antagonists, with both Pure and Bale Hounds? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Smaller one question - Are in 2ed corebook Bale Hounds at least mentioned? I know they don't get proper write-up, but at least small note about them? Like sidebar in corebook 1ed?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T02:46:20-07:00","id":282107,"title":"","content":"Thanks Acrozatarim for sharing! Looking forward to more info on the Pure and on the 2 edition itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281799#post281799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how about we get some more merits spoiled?</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> I dont know if this has been asked or even considered, but is 2 ed forsaken being kickstarted? i see a lot of the OP books are KS nowadays. Just wondering.<br /> <br /> What territories do we know will be focused on in 2 ed?<br /> I heard 2 ed is not using Colorado (done in the rockies and as a sample setting in Forsaken). Will there be anything from Canada or Northern/Eastern Europe?<br /> Loved the maps for Colorado. More maps! also spirit maps of some areas would be.. interesting, especially with places that aren't. &lt;--(gotta change the name on that one)<br /> <br /> Will there be more options to how we build Uratha in Auspices in CC? I know there was some interesting material in the players guide and signs of the moon.<br /> Interested in seeing more options per auspice. different roles that each Auspice can assume. Ex. Irraka - Stalkers. They could have different and unique roles (Shadow, Spy, Assasin , sorry for lame names, hopefully you get my drift).<br /> Similar to the Signs of the Moon perhaps, but also new variations on how auspices work.I know we got the excellent blog from Stew on some of this but.. I am hoping some more details can be spoiled? :-)<br /> <br /> Bunyip: Nice! I like the idea of new tracking rules. would like to test those very much.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T02:57:47-07:00","id":282127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282043#post282043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much i very like Acrozatarim ( you really do good work, men! ) you've become my favorite line developer! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So I can assume first supplement after the corebook would about Antagonists, with both Pure and Bale Hounds? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Smaller one question - Are in 2ed corebook Bale Hounds at least mentioned? I know they don't get proper write-up, but at least small note about them? Like sidebar in corebook 1ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things.<br /> <br /> 1. I'm not a line developer. I'm just a writer, and a new one at that. I've not even been doing this a year, yet.<br /> <br /> 2. My statements should be understood to be hypothetical (which is why I bolded that word somewhere). I don't know what supplements <b>might</b> be planned, or even <b>if</b> there are any, or anything at all. All I know is that we wrote the 2nd Edition corebook, and that hopefully we'll get more stuff down the line. That's it. So in this case, you know what I know - corebook is in process, everything else....eh? No idea.<br /> <br /> Just being clear, here. Oh, also, going from memory, I'm pretty sure the Bale Hounds are not mentioned, for reasons given a number of times in this thread (I think; it's early and I may not be fully awake yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T04:49:13-07:00","id":282167,"title":"","content":"I don't believe any of the nWoD second editions are being Kickstartered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:19:08-07:00","id":282353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=281727#post281727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because as much as Acrozatarim wants to write Pure? I want to write Bale Hounds. (Although I'd write Pure too, of course. Anything and everything <b>Werewolf</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd be up for some fresh work on Bale Hounds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282107#post282107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know if this has been asked or even considered, but is 2 ed forsaken being kickstarted? i see a lot of the OP books are KS nowadays. Just wondering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this question has come up before, and the answer is no. The new nWoD 2e cores aren't getting kickstarted afaik.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What territories do we know will be focused on in 2 ed? </div> </div> </div>I believe it has been revealed so far that, of the several hunting grounds being featured in W:tF 2e, Tokyo, Bristol and Alice Springs are included. There are several others yet to be revealed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I heard 2 ed is not using Colorado (done in the rockies and as a sample setting in Forsaken). Will there be anything from Canada or Northern/Eastern Europe? </div> </div> </div>Yes to the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:27:34-07:00","id":282363,"title":"","content":"By the way, are we going to see more Hosts, or just the Azlu and Beshilu? Any significant changes to them?<br /> After the corebook I would love to see a sourcebook on Hosts and Claimed by the way!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T10:00:46-07:00","id":282418,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's great that we have writers really interested in the Pure and the Bale Hounds. But the Hosts are cool, too. And Claimed are practically a staple (though I think you've mentioned you have stuff on them, and I know at least one has popped up in the playtesting, warning us that they're tougher).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T10:50:13-07:00","id":282502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282363#post282363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, are we going to see more Hosts, or just the Azlu and Beshilu? Any significant changes to them?<br /> After the corebook I would love to see a sourcebook on Hosts and Claimed by the way!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just Azlu and Beshilu - no space for new ones in the core - but I have added some elements to the As and Bs that I hope people will find intriguing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282418#post282418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It's great that we have writers really interested in the Pure and the Bale Hounds. But the Hosts are cool, too. And Claimed are practically a staple (though I think you've mentioned you have stuff on them, and I know at least one has popped up in the playtesting, warning us that they're tougher).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the Hosts are cool, and they're another thing I'd love the opportunity to do more work on in the future - I only had so much word count to play around with them in the core. I wrote the sections for the 'regular' antagonists (Pure, Hosts, spirits, etc) and the idigam rules, although not the sample idigam themselves, and I had a <i>lot</i> of fun doing so.<br /> <br /> As for Claimed, well, there's certainly more to them in the new core than there was in the old, but the basic stat boosts alone from Claiming are pretty monstrous, especially if you focus them heavily on physical attributes. A particular Rank 1 Spirit-Claimed ripped up an unwary Uratha really badly - it's one of the sample antagonists in the book.<br /> <br /> There's also an extra-special bonus type of Claimed in the book that is genuinely terrifying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When I say 'type' I don't mean 'type of spirit it's claimed by', either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:57:10-07:00","id":282672,"title":"","content":"More like the Uzu Siten variety of claimed? While troubling in the sense of the oath, I think the leaked Rite means there should be pretty fertile ground for playable Claimed. <br /> <br /> Sad that Claimed still get those massive attribute boosts. Then again, I was nonplussed by Ephemeral Entities still having them as well. Pretty overwhelming for anyone to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:11:48-07:00","id":282697,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that the designers are kind of in a hard spot with the werewolf genre. Basically WoD has most of the classic movie monster archetypes, which derive from European legends (except for mummies, which are 20th century). Of which werewolves are a staple.<br /> <br /> But as mentioned above, Forsaken werewolves don't really have the classic werewolf feel, because they have so much animistic material superimposed onto them.<br /> <br /> Well, the designers are, I think, kind of forced to do this. Classic werewolves are... boring? No, predicatable. Unlike vampires, which have a huge array of crazy powers, werewolves are pretty well-defined, as are there abilities. So, to make them interesting, to provide a variety of character archetypes that would parallel all the variety of vampires, artificial men, and so forth, the designers were pretty much obligated to come up with something to supplement the classic image. Which they did with the animistic/shamanistic flavor -- which does at least roughly fit the &quot;animal&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> Personally, would I would do is increase the horror aspect. Instead of making werewolves guardians against spirit incursions, make them into avatars of feral spirits themselves. Hungry spirits let lose in the world. (Or is that too vampiric?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4079-alcibiades","name":"Alcibiades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:18:56-07:00","id":282705,"title":"","content":"Can't wait to see how the Azlu and Beshilu shake out. They're so insanely awesome as antagonists. While highly focused on a role they still manage to provide unique ways of going about their evil. Something about having so many avenues to fuck with me and my group. They're just wonderful!<br /> <br /> I guess that's also a big answer on why I love Idigam as major villains. Just so many ways to screw with you, and each thing can go about it in a unique way.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, any talk among the devs of the other Ancients from the back of Predators? Idigam are a major group of them, but I think Great Big Fuck You's are great as singular Big Bads to toss about for the mythical feel of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:22:36-07:00","id":282710,"title":"","content":"They're kind of making that now, Alcibiades. Rather than being 'just' spirit cops, they are now more spirit-of-the-hunt. But still balancing that with the soul of a human.<br /> <br /> Yeah I had a lot of fun with just the three sample Azlu in a hunter game, they tore up the town, disappeared into peoples brains and lived to do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:31:43-07:00","id":282719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alcibiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282697#post282697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that the designers are kind of in a hard spot with the werewolf genre. Basically WoD has most of the classic movie monster archetypes, which derive from European legends (except for mummies, which are 20th century). Of which werewolves are a staple.<br /> <br /> But as mentioned above, Forsaken werewolves don't really have the classic werewolf feel, because they have so much animistic material superimposed onto them.<br /> <br /> Well, the designers are, I think, kind of forced to do this. Classic werewolves are... boring? No, predicatable. Unlike vampires, which have a huge array of crazy powers, werewolves are pretty well-defined, as are there abilities. So, to make them interesting, to provide a variety of character archetypes that would parallel all the variety of vampires, artificial men, and so forth, the designers were pretty much obligated to come up with something to supplement the classic image. Which they did with the animistic/shamanistic flavor -- which does at least roughly fit the &quot;animal&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> Personally, would I would do is increase the horror aspect. Instead of making werewolves guardians against spirit incursions, make them into avatars of feral spirits themselves. Hungry spirits let lose in the world. (Or is that too vampiric?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've brought it up before, so I'm not gonna go into a lot of it again.<br /> <br /> Animism definitely has it's horror aspects, though I'll admit there are hardly any mainstream sources to draw from, so I can always understand when people don't see the connection between the werewolf and other shape-shifting horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:49:17-07:00","id":282746,"title":"","content":"Yeah. There was a recent werewolf movie out called Wolfcop. More of a comedy, but still pretty bad. And the origin and lifecycle of the werewolf was pretty lame.<br /> <br /> Another one, Wer, kinda captured the feral nature of werewolves but didn't give them much more than that, so it was more of a slasher flick by the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-15-2014, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:49:27-07:00","id":282837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282746#post282746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. There was a recent werewolf movie out called Wolfcop. More of a comedy, but still pretty bad. And the origin and lifecycle of the werewolf was pretty lame.<br /> <br /> Another one, Wer, kinda captured the feral nature of werewolves but didn't give them much more than that, so it was more of a slasher flick by the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you haven't already. Check out Robert. R. McCammon's The Wolf's Hour. It's a great read about a russian born werewolf turned British spy during WW2. He has another set of short stories with the same character called The Hunter From the Woods. The werewolves in it are different but he captures a lot of themes and descriptive elements that a lot of werewolf media doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T16:16:06-07:00","id":282882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282502#post282502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also an extra-special bonus type of Claimed in the book that is genuinely terrifying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When I say 'type' I don't mean 'type of spirit it's claimed by', either.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's up Geists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T16:24:44-07:00","id":282888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282502#post282502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also an extra-special bonus type of Claimed in the book that is genuinely terrifying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When I say 'type' I don't mean 'type of spirit it's claimed by', either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifter?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T18:50:54-07:00","id":283033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282837#post282837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you haven't already. Check out Robert. R. McCammon's The Wolf's Hour. It's a great read about a russian born werewolf turned British spy during WW2. He has another set of short stories with the same character called The Hunter From the Woods. The werewolves in it are different but he captures a lot of themes and descriptive elements that a lot of werewolf media doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I read it back in the 90s and started picking up McCammon's other stuff. I particularly liked Bethany's Sin, and I haven't read his new one. I don't know if I'd completely suggest it, it's very dark, but Charlee Jacob's Symbiotic Fascination has a werewolf that, I thought, bordered on the Forsaken spirit/hunter angle. If the werewolf is part spirit, he would be part magath. There's not many good werewolf stories. If they're not a random killer type (full moon approaches, they go out and kill, either remember it or don't), they're stereotypical bikerish gangs and the alpha falls for the main character.<br /> <br /> I've been reading books about monstrous rats and spiders lately, there are a surprising amount of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T18:51:34-07:00","id":283034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=282418#post282418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It's great that we have writers really interested in the Pure and the Bale Hounds. But the Hosts are cool, too. And Claimed are practically a staple (though I think you've mentioned you have stuff on them, and I know at least one has popped up in the playtesting, warning us that they're tougher).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because I'm mostly interested in something like the Bale Hounds doesn't mean I won't write other things for the line. Remember, I said I volunteered for all the things, after all. (No, really, I very literally said that to Stew over gchat. In fact, I think I just quoted myself verbatim.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T19:06:16-07:00","id":283057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283033#post283033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I read it back in the 90s and started picking up McCammon's other stuff. I particularly liked Bethany's Sin, and I haven't read his new one. I don't know if I'd completely suggest it, it's very dark, but Charlee Jacob's Symbiotic Fascination has a werewolf that, I thought, bordered on the Forsaken spirit/hunter angle. If the werewolf is part spirit, he would be part magath. There's not many good werewolf stories. If they're not a random killer type (full moon approaches, they go out and kill, either remember it or don't), they're stereotypical bikerish gangs and the alpha falls for the main character.<br /> <br /> I've been reading books about monstrous rats and spiders lately, there are a surprising amount of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the last part of your post's angle. The media section from the original Ananasi changing breeds book recommends a book called Silk that turned out a lot better than I thought it would and has enough creepy in it for the Azilu(sp?). Sadly on werewolf fiction I keep finding myself wishing I still had my Werewolf the Apocalypse novels. Breathe Deeply was very very good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-16-2014, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T19:07:29-07:00","id":283058,"title":"","content":"Oh, I know, we just haven't heard as much on the Host front. I think just writing about Werewolf antagonists could keep you busy for a long while.<br /> <br /> So, we've got information on Bale Hounds, the Pure, spirits, shartha (azlu and beshilu, others existing even if not mentioned), claimed (different kinds) and ridden, su'ur and idigam (two kinds, do they get along?). We've spoken about tribes, auspices, lodges (mostly questions) and some hunting grounds. The Sacred Hunt and Death rage, gifts (lots of these), rites, merits and the different forms. Harmony, packs (humans, wolf blooded and possibly animal and spirit packmates), wolf-blooded and a bit about the Shadow. A tease about tracking and the supernatural senses of werewolves, a bit about fetishes and klaives and talens. I'm worried if we keep asking we won't have much to be surprised about when the book comes.<br /> <br /> Are milestone gifts still a thing?<br /> <br /> @TyrannicalRabbit I wasn't a fan of Apocalypse when it was out, but I picked up the Werewolf 20th Anthology and it was really good. Apocalypse werewolves were very physically powerful and brutal, some of the stories really show off the power very well. I'll check out Silk, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-15-2014, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T00:17:59-07:00","id":283605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283034#post283034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because I'm mostly interested in something like the Bale Hounds doesn't mean I won't write other things for the line. Remember, I said I volunteered for all the things, after all. (No, really, I very literally said that to Stew over gchat. In fact, I think I just quoted myself verbatim.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Stew pretty clearly has you, me and Acrozatarim for all the werewolf stuff, all the time. What does he even need other writers for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T01:25:09-07:00","id":283627,"title":"","content":"None of the guesses so far about the new type of Claimed are right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They aren't Geists, Siten Uzu or shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Admittedly this is slightly unfair without more context, but I'm not cleared for more spoilers at the moment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T02:53:33-07:00","id":283645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283605#post283605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Stew pretty clearly has you, me and Acrozatarim for all the werewolf stuff, all the time. What does he even need other writers for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha! Well, he does have the three of us if nobody else, that's for sure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T03:05:36-07:00","id":283647,"title":"","content":"I'll hazard a guess at the new type of claimed, you said it isn't based on the type of spirit they're possessed by, so I infer that it's the being that is being possessed. Werewolf Claimed? I forget their proper name, but I remember Predators talked about one of the Idigam being able to rip out Uratha's souls and replacing them with spirits to create claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T06:40:19-07:00","id":283812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283647#post283647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll hazard a guess at the new type of claimed, you said it isn't based on the type of spirit they're possessed by, so I infer that it's the being that is being possessed. Werewolf Claimed? I forget their proper name, but I remember Predators talked about one of the Idigam being able to rip out Uratha's souls and replacing them with spirits to create claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Idigam Claim themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T07:59:18-07:00","id":283849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283647#post283647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget their proper name, but I remember Predators talked about one of the Idigam being able to rip out Uratha's souls and replacing them with spirits to create claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are su'ur, the Empty Wolves. They're detailed in Night Horrors: Wolfsbane and have a few examples in the Rockies Hunting Ground book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T07:59:35-07:00","id":283851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283647#post283647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll hazard a guess at the new type of claimed, you said it isn't based on the type of spirit they're possessed by, so I infer that it's the being that is being possessed. Werewolf Claimed? I forget their proper name, but I remember Predators talked about one of the Idigam being able to rip out Uratha's souls and replacing them with spirits to create claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Empty Wolves are in, yes, but that's not what I was referring to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283812#post283812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can Idigam Claim themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I'm not sure how anything could Claim itself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T08:03:33-07:00","id":283853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=283851#post283851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No. I'm not sure how anything could Claim itself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> LOL I have no clue how I worded it that way.<br /> I mean can they Claim?<br /> And will they have significant differences compared to Wolfsbane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 10-16-2014, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T12:04:35-07:00","id":284015,"title":"","content":"Am I at least on to something in that it's the thing that is being possessed that makes this new type distinct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T18:09:25-07:00","id":284421,"title":"","content":"Are they spirit-claimed items or locations?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, now that I think on it. Awakened Spirits of items would very likely Claim said items if allowed to.<br /> <br /> Oh man, the shenanigans I would have with that Rite to awaken the spirits of things and convince them to help me out. Like a gritty, Disney werewolf show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 10-16-2014, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T19:31:59-07:00","id":284512,"title":"","content":"Another possiblilty: Hive-mind Claimed. One spirit, multiple bodies. Perfect foil for a pack of Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T19:56:23-07:00","id":284522,"title":"","content":"I guess a claimed inanimate object would be a fetish, right? Maybe an independent one? I know there's at least one example of multiple spirits inhabiting one body, and at least one of a moonklaive with two spirits in it. I know animals can be claimed. There's a town in Wolfsbane, Lonesome Forest, that is sort of that hive mind, a town spirit having claimed everything in the town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T07:44:50-07:00","id":284945,"title":"","content":"Let's celebrate, it is in editing!<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/editing-ho-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/editing-ho-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> Editing, ho! [Werewolf: The Forsaken] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/editing-ho-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/editing-ho-werewolf-the-forsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T03:20:06-07:00","id":285800,"title":"","content":"I got it! Spirits Claiming other spirits! It's <i>Hith</i>ception!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T04:34:19-07:00","id":285818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=284015#post284015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I at least on to something in that it's the thing that is being possessed that makes this new type distinct?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sooort of.<br /> <br /> One guess in this thread has now gone down roughly the right direction, although it's not itself correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T06:28:00-07:00","id":285840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=285818#post285818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooort of.<br /> One guess in this thread has now gone down roughly the right direction, although it's not itself correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Hith</i>ception is real?!? O_O<br /> <br /> Well, I meant it as a joke, really, though it would be awesome if it turns out that I was onto something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To elaborate, though, I had this idea of some particularly devious, parasitic spirits using Numina to hide within the corpus of other spirits, because parasites; it could be a means of disguise, feeding, getting new powers, or any combination thereof. They could have other Numina to keep their hosts completely clueless as to what's going on, a la chestbursters in Alien, or they could turn their hosts into something akin to Flayed Lunes - barely alive, barely sentient meat puppets (ephemera puppets?); the point is that they can just turn to the Uratha hunting them and be like, &quot;Oh, I'm just a totally innocent daffodil spirit, nothing to see here, move on.&quot;<br /> <br /> In any case, it would be something new to throw at werewolves, though, as I haven't seen or done anything like it in my games just yet, I'm not quite sure how it'd work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 10-18-2014, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T09:56:01-07:00","id":285988,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to elaborate a little on how The Funeral works, for pack-building. I'm very intrigued. Is the framing method an actual funeral? That certainly seems like a good one for introducing ties between people and getting everyone in a group together in one place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T10:21:52-07:00","id":285999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=285988#post285988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to elaborate a little on how The Funeral works, for pack-building. I'm very intrigued. Is the framing method an actual funeral? That certainly seems like a good one for introducing ties between people and getting everyone in a group together in one place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Each character takes their turn describing how they knew the deceased at an actual funeral, everyone plays out some scenes from the deceased's life, and that determines major dice pools, other characters in the pack, and the like. Who the deceased is, is naturally up to the players and Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T20:40:45-07:00","id":286344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=285999#post285999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Each character takes their turn describing how they knew the deceased at an actual funeral, everyone plays out some scenes from the deceased's life, and that determines major dice pools, other characters in the pack, and the like. Who the deceased is, is naturally up to the players and Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. I'm planning a campaign where the PCs are sent to join a pack where most of the Uratha members were killed. This would be an excellent method to start it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T20:56:26-07:00","id":286364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=285999#post285999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Each character takes their turn describing how they knew the deceased at an actual funeral, everyone plays out some scenes from the deceased's life, and that determines major dice pools, other characters in the pack, and the like. Who the deceased is, is naturally up to the players and Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>While aimed at Werewolf, I gotta admit that with the right crew this could set up for an interesting Descent approach as well. Do the same thing, but develop each other's player characters that way, with little moments of quantum reality changing channels moving from character to character. Once done, end the session with some form of rewind, and then see if the characters can outpace the fate the other players described.<br /> <br /> Sorry, my mind just kind of wandered there for a second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T02:27:23-07:00","id":286546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117347-idigam-chronicles-general-discussion?p=285840#post285840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Hith</i>ception is real?!? O_O<br /> <br /> Well, I meant it as a joke, really, though it would be awesome if it turns out that I was onto something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To elaborate, though, I had this idea of some particularly devious, parasitic spirits using Numina to hide within the corpus of other spirits, because parasites; it could be a means of disguise, feeding, getting new powers, or any combination thereof. They could have other Numina to keep their hosts completely clueless as to what's going on, a la chestbursters in Alien, or they could turn their hosts into something akin to Flayed Lunes - barely alive, barely sentient meat puppets (ephemera puppets?); the point is that they can just turn to the Uratha hunting them and be like, &quot;Oh, I'm just a totally innocent daffodil spirit, nothing to see here, move on.&quot;<br /> <br /> In any case, it would be something new to throw at werewolves, though, as I haven't seen or done anything like it in my games just yet, I'm not quite sure how it'd work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Hosts and Ridden already have the 'parasite' theme covered <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T06:51:58-07:00","id":286588,"title":"","content":"I really do like the idea of spirits claiming other spirits though...That could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom